hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","600 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Sufyan, from Uthman ibn Abdullah, from Aws ibn Hudhayfah, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us every night and talk to us. One night he was late for us, so we said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: A portion of the Quran came upon me, and I wanted not to go out until I completed it."
"602","601 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi, narrated to us my father, (Ha) and narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Duhaym al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Marwan ibn Muawiyah, narrated to us Abu Said ibn Awn al-Makki, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's recitation of the Quran outside the mushaf is a thousand degrees, and his recitation in the mushaf is multiplied over that up to two thousand degrees."
"603","25 - Aws ibn Abi Aws, from what he narrated: Chapter on wudu three times and prayer in sandals. 602 - Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Shubah, from al-Numan ibn Salim, he said: I heard Umar ibn Aws, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu and washed thoroughly three times. Shubah said, and he was an Arab man: I said to him: What is istawkafa? He said: He washed his hands three times."
"604","603 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Hushaym, from Yala ibn Ata, from his father, from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to a kizamah, meaning a place for purification, and perform wudu and wipe over his feet."
"605","604 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, (Ha) and narrated to us Abu Khalifah, narrated to us Abu al-Walid, narrated to us Shubah, from al-Numan ibn Salim, he said: I heard a man whose grandfather was Aws ibn Aws, from his grandfather Aws ibn Aws, he said: When he stood for prayer, he said: Hand me my sandals; then he puts them on and prays in his sandals, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"606","605 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both said: Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I saw my father wiping over the sandals, so I said: Do you wipe over them? He said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"607","606 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Sharik, from Yala ibn Ata, from Aws ibn Abi Aws, from his father, he said: We passed by a watering place of the Bedouins, and my father stood and urinated, then performed wudu and wiped over his sandals. I said: Will you not take them off? He said: I will not add for you beyond what I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing."
"608","607 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Harish, narrated to me Yahya ibn Said, from Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from his father, from Aws ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu and wipe over his sandals."
"609","608 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Yahya ibn Said, from Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from his father, from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu and wipe over his sandals, and stand for prayer."
"610","609 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Waki, from Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Ibn Abi Aws, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his sandals."
"611","610 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Waki, from Shubah, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Ibn Abi Aws, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"612","26 - Aws ibn Abdullah ibn Hajar al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him). Chapter on branding camels and where its place is on them. 611 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us al-Fayd ibn al-Wathiq al-Thaqafi, narrated to me Sakhr ibn Malik ibn Iyas ibn Malik ibn Aws ibn Abdullah ibn Hajar al-Aslami, a shaykh of the people of al-Arj, my father Malik ibn Iyas informed me, that his father Iyas ibn Malik informed him, that his father Malik ibn Aws informed him, that his father Aws ibn Abdullah ibn Hajar al-Aslami said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me, with Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), at Khadhawat between al-Juhfah and Harsha, both on one camel, heading toward Madinah. So he carried them on the stallion of his camels, Ibn al-Rida, and sent with them a servant of his called Masud, saying to him: Take them by the routes you know among the mountain paths, and do not leave them until they have finished their need of you and your camel. So he took them by Thaniyyat al-Zamha, then by Thaniyyat al-Kawbah, then he turned with them toward Ahya, then took them by Thaniyyat al-Murrah, then brought them from Shubat Dhat Kasht, then took them by al-Mudlajah, then by al-Ishalah, then by Thaniyyat al-Murrah, then brought them into Madinah, when they had finished their need of him and his camel. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Masud back to his master Aws ibn Abdullah, and he was negligent and did not brand the camels, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to command Aws to brand them on their necks with the qayd al-faras. Sakhr ibn Malik said: By Allah, that is our brand today, and qayd al-faras in my view is two rings with a line drawn extended between them."
"613","27 - Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nasri, Abu Malik ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), and he is Aws ibn al-Hadathan ibn Awf ibn Rabiah ibn Sad ibn Yarbu ibn Wathilah ibn Dahman ibn Nasr ibn Muawiyah ibn Bakr. 612 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sabiq, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and Aws ibn al-Hadathan in the days of Tashriq, and they announced that none but a believer will enter Paradise, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."
"614","613 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Shatham ibn Asil, (Ha) and narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Zayd ibn Akhzam, both said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, narrated to us Umar ibn Asbahan, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring out the charity of breaking the fast, a sa of food; and our food that day was wheat, dates and raisins. This is the wording of Zayd ibn Akhzam, and Shatham said: And our food that day was dates, raisins and aqit."
"615","28 - Aws ibn al-Samit al-Ansari, brother of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, a Badr veteran (may Allah be pleased with him). 614 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Asram ibn Fihr ibn Ghanm ibn Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Aws ibn al-Samit and his brother Ubadah."
"616","615 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj: Aws ibn al-Samit."
"617","Chapter on the expiation of zihar. 616 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, (Ha) and narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, narrated to us Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Mamar ibn Abdullah ibn Hanzalah, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, narrated to me Khuwaylah bint Thalabah, and she was the wife of Aws ibn al-Samit the brother of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, she said: He came to me one day and spoke to me about something while he was irritated, and I answered him back, so he said: You are to me as the back of my mother. Then he went out and sat in the gathering place of his people, then he returned to me and wanted me for himself, but I refused him, so he wrestled me and I wrestled him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. I said: No, by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you will not reach her until Allah judges concerning me and you. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of what I suffered from him, and he said: Your husband and your cousin, so fear Allah. And Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: Allah has heard the statement of her who disputes with you concerning her husband, until the expiation. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command him to free a slave. She said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no slave to free. He said: Then let him fast two consecutive months. She said: O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; by Allah, he cannot fast. He said: Then let him feed sixty poor persons. She said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing with which to feed. He said: We will help him with a basket of dates - and the basket holds thirty sas. I said: And I will help him with another basket. He said: You have done well; command him to give it in charity."
"618","29 - Aws al-Ansari, not attributed. Chapter: on what Allah the Mighty and Majestic has prepared for the believers on the day of breaking the fast, of honor. 617 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Jafar al-Kirmani, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Amr ibn Shamir, from Jabir, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Aws al-Ansari, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the day of breaking the fast, the angels stand at the entrances of the roads and call out: Go in the morning, O assembly of Muslims, to a Generous Lord Who bestows good and then rewards it abundantly. You were commanded to stand at night and you stood, and you were commanded to fast the day and you fasted, and you obeyed your Lord, so receive your rewards. When they have prayed, a caller calls out: Verily your Lord has forgiven you, so return rightly guided to your dwellings. It is the Day of Reward, and that day is called in the heaven the Day of Reward."
"619","618 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Muslim ibn Salim, narrated to us Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar, from Tawbah, from Said ibn Aws al-Ansari, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the morning of breaking the fast, the angels stand at the mouths of the roads and call out: O assembly of Muslims, go in the morning to a Merciful Lord Who bestows good and rewards it abundantly. You were commanded to fast the day and you fasted, and you obeyed your Lord, so receive your rewards. When they have prayed the Eid, a caller from heaven calls out: Return to your homes rightly guided; all your sins have been forgiven. And that day is called in the heaven the Day of Reward."
"620","30 - Aws ibn Shurahbil, one of Banu al-Mujammi. Chapter on the punishment of one who helps an oppressor. 619 - Narrated to us Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, narrated to us Ayyash ibn Munas, that Abu al-Hasan Nimran ibn Mikhmar narrated to him, that Aws ibn Shurahbil, one of Banu al-Mujammi, narrated to him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever walks with an oppressor to help him, while knowing he is an oppressor, has left Islam."
"621","620 - Narrated to us Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi and Ali ibn Ayyash, both said: Narrated to us Hariz ibn Uthman, narrated to us Nimran ibn Mikhmar, from Shurahbil ibn Aws, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns - he said it three times - then on the fourth kill him."
"622","31 - Aws ibn Muadh ibn Aws al-Ansari, a Badr veteran (may Allah be pleased with him). 621 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Bir Maunah: Aws ibn Muadh ibn Aws al-Ansari."
"623","622 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Aws ibn Muadh ibn Aws, he left no descendants."
"624","Aws ibn Thabit al-Ansari, an Aqabah and Badr veteran. 623 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then from Banu Amr ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, and who witnessed Badr: Aws ibn Thabit ibn al-Mundhir, a Badr veteran."
"625","624 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Aws ibn Thabit ibn al-Mundhir, he left no descendants."
"626","33 - Aws ibn al-Mundhir al-Ansari. 625 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Uhud, then from Banu al-Najjar: Aws ibn al-Mundhir."
"627","34 - Aws ibn Khawli al-Ansari, kunya Abu Layla, a Badr veteran. 626 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj: Aws ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Khawli."
"628","627 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Uqbah ibn Mukram, Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Those who descended into the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were al-Fadl, Qutham, Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Aws ibn Khawli."
"629","628 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim, narrated to me my father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: There descended into the pit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Ali ibn Abi Talib, al-Fadl and Qutham the sons of al-Abbas, and Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Layla Aws ibn Khawli said to Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with them both): I adjure you by Allah for our share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Come down. So he came down."
"630","Chapter on the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 629 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became heavy with illness, with Aishah and Hafsah present, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) entered. When he saw him, he raised his head and said: Come near me. So he leaned upon him, and remained with him until he passed away (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he had passed, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and closed the door. Al-Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) came with Banu Abd al-Muttalib and stood at the door. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) kept saying: May my father be ransom for you, pure alive and pure dead. A sweet scent spread the like of which they never found. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Admit to me al-Fadl ibn Abbas. The Ansar said: We beseech you by Allah for our share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they admitted one of them called Aws ibn Khawli, carrying a water jar in one hand. They heard a voice in the house: Do not strip the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); wash him as he is in his shirt. So Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) washed him, putting his hand under the shirt, while al-Fadl held the garment away from him, and the Ansari carried the water, with a rag on the hand of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) as he put his hand in."
"631","35 - Aws ibn Arqam al-Ansari. 630 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Uhud, then from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Aws ibn Arqam. And it is said: Sulaym Abu Kabshah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Daws; Muhammad ibn Ishaq mentioned him among those who witnessed Badr."
"632","36 - Aws ibn Yazid ibn Asram al-Ansari, an Aqabah veteran. 631 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Aws ibn Yazid ibn Asram."
"633","37 - Aws ibn Thabit al-Ansari, an Aqabah veteran, and he is the brother of Hassan ibn Thabit, and he is the father of Shaddad ibn Aws. 632 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah of the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Aws ibn Thabit."
"634","Chapter of those named Aban. 38 - Aban ibn Said ibn al-As ibn Umayyah al-Qurashi, killed on the day of Ajnadayn. 633 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those of Quraysh killed at Ajnadayn, then from Banu Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf: Aban ibn Said ibn al-As."
"635","634 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani, narrated to me Zayd ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Atash al-Sanani, narrated to me Sulayman ibn Wahb al-Janadi, from al-Numan ibn Buzruj, from Aban ibn Said ibn al-As, that he gave a sermon and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has annulled every blood claim of the Jahiliyyah."
"636","39 - Aban al-Muharibi (may Allah be pleased with him). 635 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani, narrated to us Usayd ibn Asim, narrated to us Said ibn Amir, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from al-Hakam ibn Hayyan al-Muharibi, from Aban al-Muharibi, and he was of the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Abd al-Qays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who says in the morning: Praise belongs to Allah my Lord, I associate nothing with Him, and I testify that there is no god but Allah, except that his sins continue to be forgiven until evening; and if he says it in the evening, he spends the night with his sins forgiven until morning."
"637","Chapter of those named al-Ashath. 40 - Al-Ashath ibn Qays al-Kindi, kunya Abu Muhammad. 636 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Manihi, narrated to us Isa ibn Yunus, from Ibn Awn, from al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, that Madan was disputing with a man over land, so they brought the case to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he assigned the oath to one of them. The other said: Will he take my land? He said: If he swears falsely by Allah. Ibn Awn said: And he said a stern statement."
"638","Chapter on what Allah has prepared of His punishment and anger on the Day of Resurrection for one who seizes a Muslim's wealth or swears over it with a false oath. 637 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, narrated to us al-Harith ibn Sulaym al-Kindi, narrated to us Kurdus al-Taghlibi, from al-Ashath ibn Qays al-Kindi, that a man of Kindah and a man of Hadramawt disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land in Yemen. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, my land has been seized by this one's father? So he said to the Kindi: What do you say? He said: I say my land is in my possession, I inherited it from my father. He said to the Hadrami: Do you have proof? He said: No, but let him swear, O Messenger of Allah, by Him besides Whom there is no god, that he does not know it is my land seized by his father. The Kindi prepared for the oath, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man cuts off wealth except that he will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic on the Day of Resurrection leprous. So the Kindi returned it."
"639","638 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman, (Ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, both said: Narrated to us Isa ibn Yunus, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: A man of the Hadramis disputed with a man of ours called al-Hafshish before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over his land. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Hadrami: Bring your witnesses for your right, otherwise he will swear for you. He said to him: My land is too great to not be sworn over. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The oath of a Muslim stands behind what is greater than that. So he went to swear, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he swears falsely, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will admit him into the Fire. So al-Ashath went and informed him, and he said: Make peace between me and him; so he made peace between them."
"640","639 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Bazzar al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asbati, narrated to us Safwan ibn Hubayrah, narrated to us Isa ibn al-Musayyib al-Bajali the judge, from al-Shabi, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: I once bought my oath for seventy thousand, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever cuts off the right of a Muslim by an oath will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him."
"641","640 - Narrated to us Abu Khalifah, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: Concerning me this verse was revealed: I had land in the hand of an uncle of mine, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Your proof or his oath. I said: He will swear then, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man, while he is sinful in it, will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed the verse: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to the end of the verse."
"642","641 - Narrated to us Yusuf the judge, narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, narrated to us Shubah, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: Concerning me this verse was revealed: I disputed with a man before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price."
"643","642 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him. Then al-Ashath entered and said: What did Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate to you? We said: Such and such. He said: Concerning me it was revealed: There was between me and a man a dispute over our land; we disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I had no proof. He said: Shall I make him swear? I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a man while he is sinful in it will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. And there was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to the end of the verse."
"644","643 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us al-Masudi, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: Concerning me this verse was revealed: There was between me and a man a dispute over wealth or land, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Do you have proof? I said: No. He said: Then your companion will be made to swear. He said: Then he will swear. So this verse was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to the end of the verse."
"645","644 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As informed me, Qays ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath informed me, that al-Ashath ibn Qays said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him, whether He pardons him or punishes him."
"646","Chapter. 645 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Arim, both said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, narrated to us Aqil ibn Talhah al-Sulami, from Muslim ibn Haydam, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of Kindah who did not consider me the best of them, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim that you are from us. He said: No, we are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not cast aspersion on our mother nor disown our father. Al-Ashath ibn Qays said: O Prophet of Allah, I will not hear anyone deny Quraysh from Kinanah except that I flog him."
"647","646 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, narrated to us Hushaym, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the delegation of Kindah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have children? He said: No, except a newborn born to me as I set out to you, and I would have wished to have in his place the satiation of the people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say that, for in them is the coolness of eyes and reward when they are taken, but if you say that, they are a cause of cowardice, grief and miserliness."
"648","647 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yusuf, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There was born to me from the daughter of Jamd ibn Waliah al-Kindi, and I wished we had for him a bowl of tharid. He said: Verily children are a cause of miserliness, cowardice and grief."
"649","648 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman, (Ha) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah, both said: Narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, both said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Sharik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adi al-Kindi, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most grateful of you to Allah the Mighty and Majestic is the most grateful of you to people."
"650","From the reports of al-Ashath ibn Qays. 649 - Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, narrated to us Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali, narrated to us Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: When al-Ashath ibn Qays was brought as a captive to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), he freed him from bonds and married him to his sister. Then he drew his sword and entered the camel market, and he would see no camel male or female but that he hamstrung it, and the people shouted: Al-Ashath has disbelieved. When he finished, he threw his sword and said: By Allah, I have not disbelieved, but this man married me to his sister, and had we been in our lands there would have been a wedding feast other than this. O people of Madinah, slaughter and eat, and O owners of camels, come take their price."
"651","650 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi, narrated to us Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Abu Israil al-Mulai, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I had a debt upon a man of Kindah, and I used to go to him in the early mornings, and the Fajr prayer overtook me in the mosque of al-Ashath, so I prayed. When the imam gave salam, he placed before every person a suit, sandals and five hundred dirhams. I said: I am not of the people of the mosque. He said: Even if you are not of the people of the mosque. I said: What is this? They said: Al-Ashath ibn Qays has come from Makkah."
"652","651 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, narrated to us Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi, narrated to us Ali ibn Mushir, from al-Ajlah, from al-Shabi, from Umm Hakim bint Amr ibn Sinan al-Jadaliyyah, she said: Al-Ashath ibn Qays sought permission to see Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), but Qanbar turned him back, so he bloodied his nose. Ali came out and said: What is with you and him, O Ashath? By Allah, if you had contended with the servant of Thaqif, the hairs of your backside would have bristled. It was said to him: O Commander of the Believers, who is the servant of Thaqif? He said: A boy who will rule them, leaving no Arab household but that he brings them humiliation. It was said: How long will he rule? He said: Twenty, if he reaches it."
"653","652 - Narrated to us Abu Khalifah, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam said: Nobility is only counted from just before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the time of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and continued in Islam: The house of Yemen which is in al-Suffah at the time of might in Kindah is al-Ashath ibn Qays, and its horseman among Banu Zubayd is Amr ibn Madi Karib, and its poet is Imru al-Qays of Kindah, with no disagreement on this."
"654","653 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jawhari, narrated to us Umar ibn Shabbah, narrated to me Muhammad ibn Uqbah, narrated to me Muhammad ibn Harb al-Hilali, from Isa ibn Yazid, he said: Al-Ashath sought permission to see Muawiyah, may Allah have mercy on him, in Kufa, but he kept him waiting long, while with him were Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both). He said: Is it because of these two that you veiled me, O Commander of the Believers? You know that their companion came to us and filled us with lies, meaning Ali. Ibn Abbas said: Do you think I insult you with Ibn Abi Talib? He said: No Arab better than me has been insulted. Ibn Abbas said: The servant of Mahrah killed your grandfather and stabbed the backside of your father. He said: Do you not hear what he says to me, O Commander of the Believers? He said: You began."
"655","Chapter of those named Anas. 41 - Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), kunya Abu Hamzah. 654 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani, narrated to us Waki, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Nasr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunya Abu Hamzah."
"656","655 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, narrated to us Makhul, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik and said: O Abu Hamzah."
"657","656 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us al-Haytham ibn Junadah, narrated to us Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi, narrated to us Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Nasr, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me a kunya while I was a boy. He said: And he gave me kunya by a herb I used to gather."
"658","Description of Anas ibn Malik and his appearance (may Allah be pleased with him). 657 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani, narrated to us Ismail ibn Abi Uways, narrated to us Thabit ibn Qays, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik white of head and beard, dyeing his head with henna."
"659","658 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Abu Muawiyah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) dyeing with henna."
"660","659 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Khalid ibn Uqbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us my father, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Anas ibn Malik used to yellow his beard with wars."
"661","660 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from al-Amash, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) dyeing with red."
"662","661 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, narrated to me Yahya ibn Said, my mother narrated to me, she said: I visited a co-wife of mine who was then married by Anas ibn Malik, and I saw Anas perfumed with khaluq, and he had whiteness, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for me."
"663","662 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad, narrated to us Harb ibn Maymun, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O possessor of two ears."
"664","663 - And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Sharik, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to me: O possessor of two ears."
"665","664 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Hushaym, from Abu Sasaan, from Fudayl ibn Kathir, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) had touched his forearms with khaluq because of whiteness he had."
"666","665 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai, narrated to us Talut ibn Abbad, narrated to us Salim ibn Abdullah al-Ataki, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik wearing a dark khazz cloak, a dark khazz shawl, a black turban with a tail behind him, dyeing with yellow."
"667","666 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Hushaym, from Abu Sasaan, from Fudayl ibn Kathir, he said: I saw upon Anas ibn Malik yellow khazz."
"668","667 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Harun al-Qazzaz al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sadan, from his father, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) being carried around the House by his sons on their arms, with his teeth bound with gold."
"669","668 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, narrated to me Uthman ibn Ubaydullah ibn Rafi, that he saw Abu Said al-Khudri, Jabir ibn Abdullah, Abdullah ibn Umar, Salamah ibn al-Akwa, Abu Usayd al-Badri, Rafi ibn Khadij and Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with them) trimming the mustaches like shaving, leaving the beards, and plucking the armpits."
"670","669 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar, narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, narrated to us Salm ibn Qutaybah, narrated to us Marwan ibn al-Numan, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) leaning on a staff topped with a silver fitting."
"671","670 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami, narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to me my uncle Thumamah, he said: I accompanied my grandfather Anas ibn Malik for thirty years and never saw him drink nabidh at all."
"672","671 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Saffar, narrated to us Ayyub ibn al-Najjar, judge of Yamamah, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, he said: The nabidh of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) was sweet, the lips stuck from it."
"673","672 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, narrated to us Sad ibn Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj, narrated to me my father, from his father, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) drinking tila."
"674","673 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Jumhur al-Simsar al-Tinnisi, narrated to us Abu Taqi al-Himsi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Said al-Attar al-Himsi, narrated to us Rashid ibn Rashid, he said: Anas ibn Malik had a servant who made naqaniq for him, cooked two kinds of food for him, baked hawari bread for him, and kneaded it with ghee."
"675","674 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar, narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, narrated to us Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, that Anas ibn Malik, when he completed the Quran, would gather his family and children and pray for them."
"676","675 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hisham al-Dastuwai, narrated to us Qatadah, that Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) became too weak to fast a year before his death, so he broke fast and fed a poor person each day."
"677","676 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, narrated to us Hilal ibn Yasar ibn Bawla, he said: I performed Hajj with Anas ibn Malik and saw him stop the talbiyah when he descended from the pass upon seeing the houses of Makkah."
"678","677 - Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Yaqub the judge, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated to us Abu Shihab, from Humayd, that Anas used to hasten the breaking of the fast and would not wait for the caller to prayer."
"679","678 - Narrated to us Yusuf the judge, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated to us Abu Shihab, from Humayd and Uthman al-Batti, both said: We prayed behind Anas ibn Malik the Zuhr and Asr, and we heard him reciting: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High."
"680","679 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, narrated to me my father, from Thumamah, he said: Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) would sit with a mattress spread for him to sit on, and would have his children throw before him. One day he came out to us while we were throwing and said: O my sons, evil is what you throw. Then he took and shot, and did not miss the target."
"681","680 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, (Ha) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, both said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, narrated to us Anas ibn Sirin, he said: We came with Anas from Kufa until, when we were at Atat, we awoke with the land muddy and watery, so he prayed the obligatory prayer on his mount, then said: I never prayed the obligatory prayer on my mount before today."
"682","681 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, (Ha) and narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Arim Abu al-Numan, (Ha) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, both said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, narrated to us Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I went out with Anas to the land of Baythaq Sirin until, when we were at Dijlah, Zuhr came, so he led us sitting on a mat in the ship while the ship was carrying us along."
"683","682 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Arim, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Sirin, from al-Hasan, that he stayed with Anas in Naysabur two years, and he would pray two rakahs, two rakahs."
"684","683 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Bishr al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Surayj ibn Yunus, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, that he saw Anas ibn Malik performing tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a donkey."
"685","684 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hisham al-Dastuwai, narrated to us Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray four rakahs on the day of Eid before the imam prayed."
"686","685 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hisham, narrated to us Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik used to sacrifice a camel for his sons as aqiqah."
"687","686 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hisham, narrated to us Qatadah, that Anas used to wipe over the socks."
"688","687 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hisham, narrated to us Qatadah, that Anas buried a son of his and said: O Allah, keep the earth away from his side, open the doors of heaven for his soul, and replace for him a home better than his home."
"689","688 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Kathir ibn Sulaym, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik prostrating on his turban."
"690","689 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Waki, from Said ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, that Anas recited aloud in Zuhr or Asr and did not prostrate."
"691","690 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Abu al-Yaman, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik performing voluntary prayers while traveling."
"692","691 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani, narrated to us Musa ibn Ismail, (Ha) and narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi, narrated to us Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated to us Abu Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Anas ibn Malik entered upon al-Bara ibn Malik while he was reciting poetry, and said to him: Brother, has Allah not taught you what is better for you than this? Musa ibn Ismail added in his hadith: Al-Bara said to him: Do you fear for me that I die on my bed? By Allah, that will not be Allah's trial of me, for I have killed a hundred of the polytheists, some whom I killed alone and some in whose killing I shared."
"693","692 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Al-Bara ibn Malik lay on his back then sang, so Anas said to him: Remember Allah, O my brother. So he sat upright and said: O Anas, do you think I will die on my bed, when I have killed a hundred of the polytheists in single combat, besides those in whose killing I shared?"
"694","693 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated to us Ghalib ibn Farqad al-Tahhan, he said: I was with Anas ibn Malik for two months, and he did not perform qunut in the dawn prayer."
"695","694 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated to us Ghalib ibn Farqad, that Anas ibn Malik used to give salam to his right and left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"696","695 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar, Khalid ibn Khidash informed us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Marwan ibn al-Numan narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Jusham, he said: I gave Anas ibn Malik a laxative medicine to drink."
"697","696 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi, Umm Nahar bint al-Difa narrated to us, she said: Anas ibn Malik used to pass by us when we were women and would not greet us."
"698","697 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri, narrated to us Musa ibn Ismail, narrated to us Ayan al-Jaramizi, he said: I came to Anas ibn Malik while he was in his vestibule, and I greeted him and said: May I enter? He said: This is a place where permission is not sought."
"699","698 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Sufyan, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, that he was a governor over Naysabur, and a dihqan brought him khabis in a silver vessel, so he disliked it and returned it to him; then he changed it and brought it, and he ate it."
"700","699 - Narrated to us Yusuf the judge, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated to us Abu Shihab, from Humayd, he said: We were with Anas ibn Malik, and he said: By Allah, not all that we narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did we hear from him, but we would not lie to one another."
"701","700 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar, narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari, narrated to me my uncle Thumamah, he said: Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said to us: Bind knowledge with writing."
"702","701 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that a plowman of Anas ibn Malik was working on a zurnuq, and his wife complained to Anas that he does not leave her night or day, so Anas reconciled between them upon six in each day and night."
"703","702 - Narrated to us Sahl ibn Musa al-Ramahurmuzi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Said, narrated to us Abd Rabbih ibn Abi Nafi, Raytah the umm walad of Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that Anas ibn Malik disliked bathing at midday and at the time of darkness."
"704","703 - Narrated to us Abu Ubaydullah the judge al-Ramahurmuzi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khawwat ibn Shubah, narrated to us Umar ibn Yunus, narrated to us Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I entered the house of Abu Talhah while he had locked the door upon Umm Sulaym, and she is the mother of Anas, while he was beating her. I called from behind the door: What do you want with this old woman, beating her? She called to me from behind the door and said: You say to me old woman; may Allah disable your pillar."
"705","704 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dharra, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, he said: I was in the palace with al-Hajjaj while he was parading the people because of Ibn al-Ashath, and Anas ibn Malik came until he drew near. Al-Hajjaj said to him: O wicked one, roaming in tribulation, once with Ali ibn Abi Talib, once with Ibn al-Zubayr, and once with Ibn al-Ashath. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will uproot you as the gum tree is uprooted, and I will strip you as the lizard is stripped. He said: Whom does the commander mean, may Allah set him right? Al-Hajjaj said: You I mean; may Allah deafen your hearing. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. Then he left him and said: Had I not remembered my children and feared for them, I would have spoken to him in my place words after which he would never answer me again."
"706","The age of Anas ibn Malik and his death (may Allah be pleased with him). 705 - Narrated to me Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when I was ten years old, and he passed away when I was twenty."
"707","706 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, he said: And Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, narrated to us Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Abu Khaldah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years."
"708","707 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Jubarah ibn Mughallis, narrated to us Shubayb ibn Shaybah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years."
"709","708 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years."
"710","709 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Waki, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seven years."
"711","710 - Narrated to us Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Uthman al-Massisi, Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for Anas. He said: O Allah, increase his wealth and children and bless him therein. Anas said: I have buried of my own loins, besides the children of my children, one hundred and twenty-five, and my land indeed yields twice in the year, with nothing else in the town yielding twice besides it."
"712","711 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Minjab ibn al-Harith, Ali ibn Mushir informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, he said: Aishah said: What do Abu Said and Anas know of the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They were only two small boys."
"713","712 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Hubab, Abu Abdullah Maymun narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I had a forelock, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stretch it and hold it."
"714","713 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Shaybah, narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, Abu Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was eight years old. Yazid said: Hammad ibn Salamah pointed me to this shaykh."
"715","714 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid the judge, Sharik ibn Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I washed Anas ibn Malik, and when I reached his private part, I said to his sons: You have more right to wash his private part; take it and wash it. So the one who washed it put a rag on his hand with a garment over it, then washed the private part from under the garment."
"716","715 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini, narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Humayd, he said: Anas ibn Malik passed away and there was placed in his embalming sukkah or sukk and a musk holder containing some of the sweat of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"717","716 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz al-Basri, narrated to us Hani ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: The last of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to die in Kufa was Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, and in Basra Anas ibn Malik."
"718","717 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Hassan ibn Ghalib, al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik died in the year ninety-three."
"719","718 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Jarir ibn Hazim, he said: I said to Shuayb ibn al-Habhab: When did Anas ibn Malik die? He said: In the year ninety."
"720","719 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Nasr ibn Ali, narrated to us Nuh ibn Qays, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, he said: When Anas ibn Malik died, Muwarriq al-Ijli said: Today half of knowledge has gone. It was said: How is that, O Abu al-Mutamir? He said: When a man of the people of desires opposed us in a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would say to him: Come to one who heard it from him."
"721","From what Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated. 720 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq, narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Isa ibn Musa ibn Iyas ibn al-Bukayr, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do good all your lives, and expose yourselves to the breezes of Allah's mercy, for Allah has breezes from His mercy with which He reaches whom He wills of His servants; and ask Allah to cover your faults and to secure your fears."
"722","721 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, Ibrahim ibn Suwayd narrated to us, Hilal ibn Zayd ibn Yasar narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appoint as miqats: al-Aqiq for the people of the cities, Dhat Irq for the people of Basra, Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, and al-Juhfah for the people of Sham."
"723","722 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, Hilal ibn Yasar narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): An umrah in Ramadan is like a Hajj with me."
"724","723 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, Hilal ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik in the sai around the House in the three circuits of tawaf, walking between the Yemeni corner and the Black corner in Hajj and Umrah. Then I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing."
"725","724 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai narrated to us, Abu al-Huwayrith informed me, Nuaym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir informed me, that Anas ibn Malik informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three qualities, whoever has them has tasted the flavor of faith: one to whom nothing is more beloved than Allah, one for whom to be burned by fire is more beloved than to apostatize from his religion, and one who loves for Allah and hates for Allah."
"726","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were in a house, and each one of us drew back from his seat so that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) could sit with him, so he stood at the door and said: The Imams are from Quraysh; they have a right, and I have a right, as long as they do three things: if they judge, they judge justly; if they make a covenant, they fulfill it; and if mercy is sought from them, they show mercy. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"727","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while still completing it fully."
"728","With the same chain of transmission, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and as soon as he gave the salutation he would stand up. Then I prayed with Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and when he gave the salutation he would spring up as though rising from hot stones."
"729","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj and Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Humayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between the Emigrants and the Helpers; he made brotherhood between Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. Sa'd said to him: I have wealth, and it is shared between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them you prefer so that I may divorce her, and when she is free, marry her. He said: I have no need of your wealth or your family; direct me to the market. So he went and then returned having earned dates and dried yogurt. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a trace of yellow perfume on him, and he said: What is this? He said: I have married a woman of the Helpers. He said: What did you give her as dower? He said: The weight of a date-pit of gold - or a date-pit of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."
"730","With the same chain of transmission, he said: I attended a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there was neither bread nor meat. I said: What was it, O Abu Hamzah? He said: Sawiq (parched barley drink) and dates."
"731","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us: Hammad ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A bird was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed before him, and he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me. Then Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) came and knocked on the door. I said: Who is it? He said: I am Ali. I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is occupied. So he went back three times, coming each time. He said: Then he struck the door with his foot and entered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What kept you? He said: I came three times, and each time he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is occupied. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What made you do that? I said: I had hoped it would be a man of my tribe."
"732","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pressed his eye to a palm-stalk hut to peep in. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and aimed at him with a stick or a piece of iron to poke out his eye with it. When he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he drew back. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Had you remained still, I would have poked out your eye."
"733","With the same chain of transmission: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah will shake with three quakes, and every hypocrite and disbeliever will come out of it."
"734","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Anas, in a raised (marfu') report, who said: There is no ruqyah (healing incantation) except for the evil eye, or a venomous sting, or blood that does not stop flowing."
"735","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us: Sulayman Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Qudamah, from Anas, who said: The most beloved fragrant plant to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was al-faghiyah (henna blossom)."
"736","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Yahya al-Qurashi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr Abu Sahl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Helpers, and the children of the Helpers, and the grandchildren of the Helpers, and the daughters-in-law and the neighbors."
"737","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not enter upon women, even if they are your daughters-in-law. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the hamw (the husband's male relatives)? He said: Their hamw is death."
"738","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the cooking pots on the day of Khaybar to be overturned, emptying them of donkey meat."
"739","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Sharik, from al-A'mash, from Yazid ibn Aban, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qur'an is wealth; there is no poverty after it, and no wealth apart from it."
"740","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hasan, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim quietly, and so did Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"741","Ja'far ibn Sulayman ibn Hajib al-Antaki al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Hasan al-Basri, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I go out with you to battle? He said: O Umm Salamah, jihad has not been prescribed for women. She said: I will treat the wounded, tend the eyes, and give water to drink. He said: Then yes."
"742","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Imran ibn Maysarah al-Adami narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-Awwam ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four things are not attained except with striving in wonder: patience, which is the beginning of worship; humility; remembrance of Allah; and having little (of worldly provision)."
"743","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: al-Nu'man ibn Shibl narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is equal to half the prayer of one standing."
"744","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two (fingers)."
"745","Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us: Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Gabriel (peace be upon him) took out his innards into a basin of gold and washed it, then filled it with wisdom and light - or wisdom and knowledge."
"746","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Umar ibn Abi al-Rutayl narrated to us: Habib ibn Khalid al-Asadi narrated to us, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn al-Mughirah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, and we went out with him. We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anxious and intensely grieved, and we would not speak to him until we reached the grave, and it was not yet finished being dug as a lahd (niche grave). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat down and we sat around him; he spoke to himself for a while and kept looking at the sky. Then the grave was finished, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended into it, and I saw him growing more grieved. Then he finished and came out, and I saw that his distress had been lifted from him and he smiled (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you anxious and grieved such that we could not speak to you, then we saw your distress lifted - why was that? He said: I was remembering the narrowness and distress of the grave and the weakness of Zaynab, and that weighed upon me. So I supplicated to Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He) to lighten it for her, and He did. She was indeed squeezed with a squeeze heard by all between the horizons except the jinn and mankind."
"747","Salih ibn Shu'ayb al-Basri narrated to us: Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Ammar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is made in a village, Allah grants it safety from His punishment on that day."
"748","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday between the Asr prayer and the setting of the sun; and it is about this much - meaning, a handful."
"749","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us: Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father died and did not perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: What do you think - if your father had a debt and you paid it, would it be settled on his behalf? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"750","Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us: Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my community."
"751","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Abu Hashim, the dealer in saffron, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him: Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) came with a piece of bread to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is this? She said: A loaf I baked, and I could not feel at ease until I brought you this piece. He said: It is indeed the first food to enter your father's mouth in three days."
"752","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Athram narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not believed in me who sleeps his night satiated while his neighbor is hungry beside him and he knows of it."
"753","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, and from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast to one another about mosques."
"754","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us: Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him before his death."
"755","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Nuh ibn Abbad al-Qurashi al-Basri narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A servant attains by good character the great ranks of the Hereafter and the noble stations, even if his worship is weak; and he attains by bad character the lowest rank in Hell."
"756","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Salamah ibn Subayh al-Yuhmadi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman performs ghusl after her menstruation, she should undo her hair and wash it with khitmi (marshmallow plant) and ushnan (alkali plant); and when she performs ghusl after major ritual impurity, she should pour water over her head and squeeze it."
"757","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Azraq narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Some eloquent speech is magic, and some poetry is wisdom."
"758","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enjoin gift-giving as a bond between people, and he would say: If only people would accept Islam, they would exchange gifts without hunger (i.e., not out of need)."
"759","Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Ufayr ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Gabriel (peace be upon him) comes to me in the form of Dihyah al-Kalbi. Anas said: Dihyah was a handsome, fair-complexioned man."
"760","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion."
"761","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Qazzaz narrated to us: Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Render the trust to whoever entrusted you, and do not betray whoever betrayed you."
"762","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa al-Dimashqi, from Thabit al-Bunani, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him: Some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Fix prices for us, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The highness and lowness of your prices is in the Hand of Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He). I hope to meet Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He) with none of you having a claim of injustice against me regarding wealth or blood."
"763","Anas ibn Malik al-Qushayri, whose kunyah was Abu Umayyah - also said to be Abu Mayyah - used to reside in Basra. Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Umayyah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a journey, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Come and eat lunch. I said: I am fasting. He said: Shall I not tell you about the traveler? Allah has lifted fasting from him, and half of the prayer."
"764","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of Banu Amir: A man called Anas ibn Malik narrated to him that he came to Madinah and entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need of his, and found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Come near. The man said: I am fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has lifted fasting from the traveler, and half of the prayer, and from the pregnant woman and the nursing mother."
"765","Musa ibn Harun and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of Banu Amir - Ayyub said: Abu Qilabah said to me: He is alive, so meet him and hear the hadith from him. Ayyub said: So I met al-Amiri, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out horsemen who raided the camels of a neighbor of ours and took them away. So he set out regarding that - either he said: my father, or he said: my uncle, or he said: a near relative of his - and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. He said: I came to him while he was eating, and he said: Come to lunch. I said: I am fasting. He said: Come, let me tell you about that. Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He) has lifted fasting from the traveler, and half of the prayer, and from the pregnant woman - or he said: the nursing mother. And he ordered the camels to be returned. Whenever he narrated this hadith, he would regret it and say: If only I had eaten of the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"766","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; and al-Hadrami narrated to us: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn al-Makki narrated to us: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari and Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sawadah, from Anas ibn Malik, a man of Banu Ka'b, who said: Horsemen of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided us. I came to him while he was eating, and he said: Sit and partake of this food of ours. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am fasting. He said: Sit, let me tell you about the prayer and about fasting. Allah has lifted half - or a half - of the prayer from the traveler, and lifted fasting from the traveler, the sick person, and the pregnant woman. By Allah, he said all of them, or one of them. So I blamed myself for not having eaten of the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"767","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Ibn Sawadah al-Qushayri, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Horsemen of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided us, so I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating, and he said: Sit and partake of our food. I said: I am fasting. He said: Sit, let me tell you about the prayer and about fasting. Allah has lifted half of the prayer from the traveler, and lifted fasting from the traveler and from the nursing mother. So I blamed myself for not having eaten of the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"768","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from a man of theirs: He entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating, and he said: Come. He said: I am fasting. He said: Come, let me tell you. Allah has lifted fasting from the traveler, and half of the prayer."
"769","Anas ibn al-Nadr al-Ansari, the paternal uncle of Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him). Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: Al-Rubayyi', the daughter of al-Nadr, his paternal aunt, slapped a slave girl and broke her tooth. They offered them blood-money and they refused; they sought pardon and they refused. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered them to apply retaliation. Then her brother Anas ibn al-Nadr came and said: O Messenger of Allah, will the tooth of al-Rubayyi' be broken? No, by the One who sent you with the truth, her tooth shall not be broken. He said: O Anas, the Book of Allah prescribes retaliation. Then the people pardoned. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear by Allah, Allah fulfills their oath."
"770","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik: His uncle Anas ibn al-Nadr was absent from the fighting at Badr, and he said: I was absent from the first fighting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against the polytheists; if Allah lets me witness with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah will surely see what I do. When the day of Uhud came, he met the polytheists while the people were routed, and he said: O Allah, I apologize to You for what these have done - meaning the Muslims - and I disavow to You what these have brought - meaning the polytheists. Then he took his sword and met Sa'd ibn Mu'adh and said: O Sa'd, I smell the fragrance of Paradise from beyond Uhud. He went forward and was killed, and he was not recognized until his sister recognized him by the beauty of his fingertips. He had more than eighty wounds of spear thrusts, sword strikes, and arrow shots."
"771","Anas ibn Mu'adh ibn Aws al-Ansari. Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Helpers martyred on the day of the Trench: Anas ibn Mu'adh ibn Aws ibn Abd Amr."
"772","Anas ibn Aws al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of the Bridge from the Helpers, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Anas ibn Aws."
"773","Chapter: Those named Unays. Anas ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi - also said to be Unays - whose kunyah was Abu Zayd. Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Missisi narrated to us: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: al-Saluli narrated to me that Sahl ibn al-Hanzaliyyah narrated to him that they marched with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar - and he mentioned the hadith. Its completion is to be written in the chapter of Sin: Sahl ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. To be written in the chapter of Za: Zayd ibn Rafi', the story of the stoning."
"774","Unays ibn Junadah al-Ghifari, the brother of Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him). Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn A'idh narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abu Tarfah Abbad ibn al-Rayyan al-Lakhmi narrated to us, saying: I heard Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi say: Amir ibn Ludayn, the judge of the people under Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Layla al-Ash'ari say: Abu Dharr narrated to me, saying: The first thing that called me to Islam was that we were Bedouin people struck by a year of drought. So I carried my mother and my brother - whose name was Unays - to in-laws of ours in upper Najd. When we alighted with them, they honored us. When a man of the tribe saw that, he went to my maternal uncle and said: Do you know that Unays visits your wife in your absence? It sank into his heart. I returned from pasturing my camels and found him gloomy, weeping. I said: Why are you weeping, O uncle? He told me the news. I said: Allah forbid that; we detest indecency, even if hard times have befallen us. You have spoiled for us the good cheer with which you received us, and there is no way to stay together. So I carried my mother and my brother until we alighted near Makkah. My brother said: I am going to contend in verse with a poet. I said: Do not do it. But contentiousness drove him until he vied with Durayd ibn al-Simmah, his flock against his flock. By Allah, Durayd that day was more poetic than my brother. They sought judgment from al-Khansa, and she preferred my brother over Durayd - that was because Durayd had proposed to her through her father, and she said: He is an old man; I have no need of him - so she held that against him. So we joined his flock to ours, and we had a large herd. He said: Then I came to Makkah and began at al-Safa, where there were men of Quraysh. It had reached me that among them was a Sabian, or a madman, or a poet, or a sorcerer. I said: Where is this one you speak of? They said: There he is, where you see. I turned toward him, and by Allah, I had not gone past them the throw of a stone before they pelted me with every bone, stone, and clod, and covered me in my own blood. I came to the House and entered between the curtains and the structure, and fasted there for thirty days, neither eating nor drinking except from the water of Zamzam, until on a bright moonlit night two women of Khuza'ah came and circumambulated the House, then mentioned Isaf and Na'ilah - two idols they used to worship. I stuck my head out from under the curtains and said: Put one of them upon the other. They became angry, then said: By Allah, if our men were present, you would not have said this. Then they turned away. I went out following their tracks until they met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Who are you two, and from where are you, and from where have you come, and what has brought you? They told him the news. He said: Where did you leave the Sabian? They said: We left him between the curtains and the structure. He said to them: Did he say anything to you? They said: Yes, a word that fills the mouth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. Then they slipped away, and I came to where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, and greeted him then. He said: Who are you, and from whom are you, and from where are you, and from where have you come, and what has brought you? I began to tell him the news. He said: From where did you eat and drink? I said: From the water of Zamzam. He said: It is indeed nourishing food. With him was Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to give him supper. He said: Yes. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out walking, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) took my hand until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at the door of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). Then Abu Bakr entered his house, and raisins of Ta'if were brought, and he kept throwing them to us handful by handful, and we ate of them until we were full. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service. He said: A land has been shown to me, a land with water - I think it is none but Tihamah. So go out to your people and call them to what you have entered into. He said: So I went out until I came to my mother and my brother and told them the news. They said: We have no aversion to the religion you have entered into - and they accepted Islam. Then we went out until we came to Madinah, and I informed my people. They said: We believe you, but let us meet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and met him, Ghifar said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Dharr told us what you told him, and we have accepted Islam and testify that you are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Aslam and Khuza'ah came forward and said: O Messenger of Allah, we desire and have entered into what our brothers and allies have entered into. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam - may Allah grant them safety - and Ghifar - may Allah forgive them. Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) took my hand and said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service, O Abu Bakr. He said: Did you used to worship in your pre-Islamic days? I said: Yes; you would have seen me standing at the sun, remaining in prayer until its heat hurt me, then falling as though I were a hidden shelter. He said to me: In which direction did you face? I said: I do not know, except where Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He) directed me, until Allah brought Islam to me."
"775","Unays ibn Atik ibn Amir al-Ansari - also said to be Aws. Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of the bridge of al-Mada'in from the Helpers, from Banu Abd al-Ashhal then Banu Za'ura': Unays ibn Atik ibn Amir."
"776","Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of the Bridge from the Helpers, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then from Banu Za'ura': Aws ibn Atik ibn Amir."
"777","Unays ibn Mu'adh ibn Qays al-Ansari, a veteran of Badr. Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Helpers, from Banu Amr ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar then from Banu Qays ibn Ubayd ibn Zayd ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Amr ibn Malik: Unays ibn Mu'adh ibn Qays."
"778","Unays ibn Qatadah al-Ansari, a veteran of Badr. Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Uhud from the Helpers, then from Banu Zurayq: Unays ibn Qatadah."
"779","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Helpers, then from al-Aws: Unays ibn Qatadah."
"780","Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he was the one who announced permission for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he witnessed Badr. Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, saying: His freedman - meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - used to give him permission to enter."
"781","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"782","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"783","Chapter: Those named Iyas. Iyas ibn Abd al-Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him). Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us; and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us; and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Minhal, from Iyas ibn Abd al-Muzani, who was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of water."
"784","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Minhal, from Iyas ibn Abd al-Muzani: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of water."
"785","Iyas ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Dhubab. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Iyas ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not beat the female servants of Allah. He said: Then the women became emboldened and their manners toward their husbands worsened. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, the women have become emboldened and their manners toward their husbands have worsened since you forbade beating them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then beat them. So the people beat the women that night, and many women came complaining of beating. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Last night seventy women gathered around the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), all of them complaining of beating. By Allah, you will not find those (who beat) to be the best of you."
"786","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us; and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Iyas ibn Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not beat the female servants of Allah. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the women have become emboldened toward their husbands since you forbade beating them. So he permitted them and they beat. Many women - seventy women - gathered around the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each complaining of her husband; and you will not find those to be the best of you."
"787","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Iyas ibn Abi Dhubab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not beat the female servants of Allah. So they stopped beating them. Then Umar came and said: By Allah, the women have become emboldened toward their husbands. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered beating them. Many women gathered around the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When morning came, he said: Last night seventy women have gone around the family of Muhammad, each complaining of beating. By Allah, I do not consider those to be the best of you."
"788","Iyas ibn Mu'awiyah al-Muzani. Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Dustuwa'i narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Iyas ibn Mu'awiyah al-Muzani: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is a must, even if (the reward of) a she-camel, even if (the time of) milking a sheep; and whatever is after the last evening prayer (Isha) is of the night."
"789","Iyas ibn Tha'labah Abu Umamah al-Balawi. Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Munib ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umamah ibn Tha'labah narrated to us: my father informed me, saying: I left the mosque and there was a man in white clothes, a shirt and a cloak, who said to me: My grandfather Abu Umamah ibn Tha'labah informed me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Simplicity in dress is part of faith; simplicity in dress is part of faith; simplicity in dress is part of faith."
"790","Al-Husayn ibn al-Samayda' al-Antaki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Hakim ibn Hizam: Abu al-Munib ibn Abi Umamah informed him that he met Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik. My father narrated to me, saying: We were in a gathering recalling worldly matters, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Simplicity in dress is part of faith - three times."
"791","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam informed us: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, that Abdullah ibn Abi Umamah ibn Tha'labah narrated to him, from his father, that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Simplicity in dress is part of faith; simplicity in dress is part of faith."
"792","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Asim ibn Anbasah al-Abbadani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Humran narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Tha'labah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: I heard your father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Simplicity in dress is part of faith - meaning austerity."
"793","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Munib al-Madani narrated to us, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Abi Umamah, from Abu Umamah ibn Tha'labah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed them of going out to Badr, and he resolved to go out with him. His maternal uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar said to him: Stay with your mother, O son of my sister. Abu Umamah said: Rather you stay with your sister. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered Abu Umamah to remain with his mother, and he went out with Abu Burdah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and she had died, so he prayed over her."
"794","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Aslami narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Munib ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umamah al-Balawi narrated to us - whose name was Iyas ibn Tha'labah and who had accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Abi Umamah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to perform ablution from ghamr (greasiness of meat), and that none of us should harm another."
"795","Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Munib narrated to us, from his grandfather, from his father Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit cross-legged (al-qurfusa')."
"796","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Munib narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Atiyyah ibn Abdullah ibn Unays, that he said: Abu Umamah ibn Tha'labah informed us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes others than his rightful patrons as patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf (supererogatory act) nor adl (obligatory ransom) will be accepted from him. Whoever swears at this pulpit of mine a false oath by which he misappropriates the wealth of a Muslim man without right, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him. Whoever introduces an innovation (hadath) in this city of mine, or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah will not accept from him sarf or adl."
"797","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja informed us: Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam informed us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed him, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, that he heard Abu Umamah ibn Tha'labah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has made the Fire obligatory for him and forbidden Paradise to him. A man said: Even if it is something small, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if it is a stick of arak wood."
"798","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Malik informed us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him. They said: Even if it is something small, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Even if it is a stick of arak wood - he said it three times."
"799","Abu Urubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu al-Mu'afa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b, from Abdullah ibn Ka'b, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seizes by his oath the right of a Muslim man, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him. A man stood up and said: Even if it is something small? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if it is a stick of arak wood."
"800","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir: Muhammad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to him that he heard his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b narrate that Abu Umamah ibn Tha'labah al-Harithi narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man seizes the right of a Muslim man by his oath except that Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him. A man of the people said: Even if it is small, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Even if it is a tooth-stick of arak wood."
"801","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated to us: Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b: his brother Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to him that he heard Abu Umamah al-Harithi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man seizes the right of a Muslim man by his oath except that Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him. A man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small? He said: Even if it is a tooth-stick of arak wood."
"802","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Asim ibn Anbasah al-Abbadani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Humran narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Abdullah ibn Tha'labah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, that he said: I heard your father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by a false oath, it will be a black spot on his heart which nothing will remove until the Day of Resurrection."
"803","Iyas ibn Aws al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Uhud from the Helpers, then from Banu Mu'awiyah ibn Awf: Iyas ibn Aws."
"804","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Uhud from the Helpers, then from Banu al-Nabit: Iyas ibn Aws."
"805","Iyas ibn Wadhaqah al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). Al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Yamamah from the Helpers, then from Banu Salim ibn Awf: Iyas ibn Wadhaqah."
"806","Iyas ibn Mu'adh al-Ansari. Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid, of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, who said: When Abu al-Haysar Anas ibn Rafi' came to Makkah with youths of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, among them Iyas ibn Mu'adh, seeking an alliance from Quraysh against their people of the Khazraj, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard of them and came to them and sat with them and said: Would you like something better than what you came for? They said: What is that? He said: I am the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); He sent me to the servants to call them to worship Him and not associate anything with Him, and Allah has revealed the Book to me. Then he explained Islam to them and recited the Qur'an to them. Iyas ibn Mu'adh - who was a young lad - said: O my people, by Allah, this is better than what you came for. Abu al-Haysar Anas ibn Rafi' took a handful of the pebbles of al-Batha and struck Iyas in the face with it and said: Leave us alone; by my life, we came for something other than this. Iyas fell silent, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got up from them. They returned to Madinah, and the battle of Bu'ath occurred between al-Aws and al-Khazraj. Then Iyas ibn Mu'adh did not live long before he died. Mahmud ibn Labid said: Those of his people who attended him at his death informed me that they kept hearing him declare the oneness of Allah, magnify Him, praise Him, and glorify Him until he died; they had no doubt that he died a Muslim. He had indeed taken Islam to heart in that sitting when he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he heard."
"807","Abyad ibn Hammal al-Mazini al-Saba'i. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Faraj ibn Sa'id ibn Alqamah ibn Sa'id ibn Abyad ibn Hammal al-Mazini al-Saba'i narrated to us: my uncle Thabit ibn Sa'id ibn Abyad ibn Hammal narrated to me, that Sa'id ibn Abyad ibn Hammal narrated to him, from his father Abyad ibn Hammal: He spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about charity when he came to him in Madinah as a delegate. He said: O brother of Saba, charity is a must. He said: Our crop is only cotton, O Messenger of Allah; Saba has dispersed and none remain of them except a few in Ma'rib. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a settlement with Abyad ibn Hammal for seventy garments of the choicest value of Ma'afiri cloth each year on behalf of those remaining of Saba in Ma'rib. They kept paying it until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"808","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Faraj ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his uncle Thabit ibn Sa'id, from his father Sa'id, from Abyad ibn Hammal: He accepted Islam along with three brothers of Kindah who had been his slaves in the pre-Islamic era. He came as a delegate to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), with one of them serving him. The servant spoke to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) during his caliphate, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) called Abyad ibn Hammal and asked him to free the one who served him, and to buy from him his two brothers in Ma'rib for six non-Arab captives of the Qadisiyyah spoils. Abyad ibn Hammal did that: he freed the one who was with him and took in place of his two brothers six non-Arab captives of the Qadisiyyah spoils. He said: The delegation of Abyad ibn Hammal to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was because the officials had encroached upon them after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away regarding the seventy garments of the settlement Abyad ibn Hammal had made with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) confirmed that as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had fixed it, until Abu Bakr died. When Abu Bakr died, that was annulled and it returned to ordinary charity."
"809","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us: Faraj ibn Sa'id ibn Alqamah ibn Sa'id ibn Abyad ibn Hammal narrated to us: my uncle Thabit ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from his father Sa'id, from his father Abyad ibn Hammal: He requested as a grant the salt of Ma'rib called Shadhdha from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he granted it to him. Then al-Aqra' ibn Habis al-Tamimi said: O Prophet of Allah, I have come to salt in the pre-Islamic era; it is in a land where whoever comes to it takes of it, and it is like ever-flowing water. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abyad ibn Hammal to rescind his grant. Abyad said: I rescind it on condition that it be counted from me as charity. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity from you, and it is like ever-flowing water; whoever comes to it takes of it. He said: So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land and pasture at al-Jurf - the Jurf of Murad - in the place where he rescinded it from him. And he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the protected preserve (hima) of arak trees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no preserve in arak trees. He said: An arak tree in my enclosure (khitari). He said: There is no preserve in arak trees. Faraj said - meaning Abyad: In my khitari means: the land in which there is crops fenced around it."
"810","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr al-Tannuri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Qays al-Ma'ribi narrated to us, from his father, from Sumayy ibn Qays, from Thumamah ibn Sharahil, from Shumayr, from Abyad ibn Hammal: He came as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) requesting the salt as a grant, and he granted it to him. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you have granted him? Ever-flowing water. So he took it back from him. And I asked him what of arak trees may be made a preserve? He said: What the hooves of camels do not reach."
"811","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us; and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Qays ibn Hafs al-Darimi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Qays al-Ma'ribi narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Thumamah ibn Sharahil, from Shumayr ibn Abd al-Madan, from Abyad ibn Hammal: He came as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he granted him the salt. When he turned away, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you have granted him? You have only granted him ever-flowing water. He said: So he took it back. He said: And I asked him what of arak trees may be made a preserve? He said: What the hooves of camels do not reach."
"812","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Qays al-Ma'ribi narrated to us, saying: I heard my father mention, from Thumamah ibn Sharahil, from Sumayy ibn Qays, from Abyad ibn Hammal: He came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and requested as a grant the salt of Ma'rib, and he granted it to him. A man said: Do you know, O Messenger of Allah, what you have granted him? You have granted him ever-flowing water. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it back from me. He said: And I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what of arak trees may be made a preserve? He said: A preserve is what the hooves of camels do not reach."
"813","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Madani narrated to us: Faraj ibn Sa'id narrated to us: my uncle Thabit ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from his father Sa'id ibn Abyad ibn Hammal: He had a rash on his face - meaning qawba' (ringworm) - and I disliked his nose. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and wiped over his face, and that evening did not come upon him with any trace of it remaining."
"814","Ahmar ibn Jaz' al-Sadusi. Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; and Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Bakkar ibn Muhammad al-Sirini narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Rashid informed us, from al-Hasan, saying: Ahmar ibn Jaz', the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, saying: We used to take cover for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he held his hands away from his sides when he prostrated."
"815","Asmar ibn Mudarris. Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: Umm Janub bint Shumaylah narrated to me, from her mother Suwaydah bint Jabir, from her mother Uqaylah bint Asmar ibn Mudarris, from her father Asmar ibn Mudarris, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him. He said: Whoever gets first to what no Muslim has gotten to before him, it is his. So the people went out racing, drawing lines (to mark land)."
"816","Al-Aswad ibn Khalaf al-Khuza'i. Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, that Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed him, that his father al-Aswad attended the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving pledge to the people at Qarn Masqalah - he said: Qarn Masqalah is toward the houses of Abu Thumamah; that part of it facing the house of Ibn Amir, and the part behind it facing the house of Ibn Samurah and its surroundings. Al-Aswad said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving pledge to the people; men, women, young, and old came and pledged to him upon Islam and the testimony. I said: What is the testimony? Muhammad ibn al-Aswad informed me, saying: Upon the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."
"817","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf, from his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to renew the boundary markers of the Sanctuary in the year of the Conquest."
"818","Aswad ibn Asram al-Muharibi. Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us; and Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi, from Aswad ibn Asram al-Muharibi: He came with fat camels of his to Madinah in a time of drought and barrenness of the land. When the people of Madinah saw them, they marveled at their fatness. I mentioned that to the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for them and they were brought. He went out to them and looked at them and said: Why did you bring these camels of yours? He said: I wanted a servant in exchange for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who has a servant? Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then bring her. Uthman brought her, and when Aswad saw her, he said: One like her is what I want. He said: You have her, so take her. Aswad took her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his camels. Aswad said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Do you control your tongue? He said: What would I control if I did not control it? He said: Do you control your hand? He said: What would I control if I did not control my hand? He said: Then do not say with your tongue except what is good, and do not extend your hand except to good."
"819","Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ali al-Qurashi, from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi: Aswad ibn Asram al-Muharibi narrated to me, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Do you control your hand? I said: What would I control if I did not control my hand? He said: Do you control your tongue? He said: What would I control if I did not control my tongue? He said: Do not extend your hand except to good, and do not say with your tongue except what is good."
"820","Al-Aswad ibn Sari' al-Mujashi'i. Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I used to recite poetry to him - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and I did not know his Companions until a man came, broad between the shoulders, bald. It was said to me: Be quiet, be quiet. I said: Alas, who is this for whom I must be silent before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? It was said: He is Umar ibn al-Khattab. I knew afterwards, by Allah, that had he heard me, he would not have hesitated to take me by the leg and drag me to al-Baqi'."
"821","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I was a poet, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not recite to you praises with which I have praised my Lord (Exalted and Majestic is He)? He said: Your Lord indeed loves praise - but he did not ask me for more."
"822","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us; and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Sawwar al-Anbari narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Muzani narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: al-Aswad ibn Sari' said: Shall I not recite to you praises with which I have praised my Lord? He said: Your Lord indeed loves praise - and he did not ask him for more than that."
"823","Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: al-Aswad ibn Sari' was a poet. He said: O Prophet of Allah, shall I not let you hear praises with which I have praised my Lord? He said: Your Lord indeed loves praise - or: nothing is more beloved to Him than praise from Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He)."
"824","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have praised my Lord with praises. He said: Your Lord indeed loves praise - and he did not ask him to recite."
"825","Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Amir ibn Salih narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not recite to you praises with which I have praised my Lord (Exalted and Majestic is He)? He said: Your Lord indeed loves praise - and he did not ask me for more."
"826","Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb informed us: Yunus narrated to us, and another whom he named, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have praised you with praises. He said: Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He) indeed loves to be praised - and he did not ask him to recite."
"827","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: Ya'la ibn Abbad ibn Ya'la narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and their killing reached the point that they killed the offspring of the polytheists. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with people whose killing reaches the point that they killed the offspring of the polytheists? They said: O Messenger of Allah - and he mentioned a phrase after it - and he said: Are not the best of you the children of the polytheists? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no child is born except upon the fitrah (natural disposition), until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."
"828","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab and Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, both saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya Abu al-Haytham - who was intelligent: al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sari' - who was a poet, and was the first to tell stories in this mosque - who said: Killing among them reached the point that they killed the offspring. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Are not the best of you the children of the polytheists? There is no child born except upon the fitrah of Islam, until he speaks clearly; then his parents make him a Jew, or a Christian, or a Magian."
"829","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us: al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah until his tongue speaks clearly; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."
"830","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and victory was granted them. Some people took to killing children. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with people whose killing has gone so far that they killed the offspring? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, they are only the children of the polytheists. He said: The best of you are the children of the polytheists. Beware, the offspring are not to be killed. Every soul is born upon the fitrah until its tongue speaks clearly; then its parents make it a Jew or a Christian."
"831","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us; and Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and their killing led them to kill the offspring. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with people whose killing led them to kill the offspring? A man said: Are they not the children of the polytheists? He said: Are not the best of you the children of the polytheists? Every child is born upon the fitrah until his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian - and the wording is that of al-Muqaddami's hadith."
"832","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Rawh ibn Hatim al-Judhu'i narrated to us: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': They raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and met the enemy and killed until they reached the offspring. They asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Every child is upon the fitrah until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."
"833","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us: Sallam narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, Yunus, and Hisham, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and their killing led them to kill children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What is with the children? They said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not of their fathers? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are not the best of you the children of the polytheists? Every soul is born upon the fitrah until its tongue speaks clearly."
"834","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ishkab narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no soul born except upon the fitrah until its tongue speaks clearly."
"835","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment; they met the enemy and kept killing until they reached the children. When the detachment returned, that was reported to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did I not forbid you? They said: They are only the children of the polytheists. He said: Are not the best of you the children of the polytheists? Then he ordered a caller who called out: Beware, every child is born upon the fitrah."
"836","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Anbasah al-Ghanawi, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened in killing until their killing of children was reached. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."
"837","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fudalah, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none who loves praise more than Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He), and none who has more excuses (for His servants) than Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He)."
"838","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid al-Attar narrated to us: Ma'mar ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: When Uthman ibn Maz'un died, the Muslims grieved for him. When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, he said: He has joined our righteous predecessor Uthman ibn Maz'un."
"839","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us: Sallam ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is in Paradise? He said: The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and the newborn child is in Paradise."
"840","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us: Sallam ibn Miskin and Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: A captive was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I repent to Allah, and I do not repent to Muhammad. He said: He has recognized the right for its people."
"841","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Sallam ibn Miskin, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a captive, and he said: O Allah, I repent to You, and I do not repent to Muhammad. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has recognized the right for its people."
"842","Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Aswad ibn Sari'. Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four on the Day of Resurrection will argue with proof: a deaf man who does not hear, a foolish man, an aged man, and one who died in the interval (fatrah). As for the deaf man, he will say: O Lord, the youths pelted me with dung. As for the aged man, he will say: Islam came and I did not understand. As for the one who died in the interval, he will say: Lord, no messenger of Yours came to me. So He will take their covenants that they will obey Him. Then He will send a messenger to them: Enter the Fire. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if they entered it, it would be cool and safe for them."
"843","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari'. Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have praised Allah with praise, and praised you with praise. He said: Bring it, and begin with the praise of Allah."
"844","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah - and he mentioned something similar."
"845","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ma'mar ibn Bakkar al-Sa'di narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari' al-Tamimi, who said: I came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have composed verse in which I praised Allah (Exalted and Majestic is He) and praised you. He said: As for what you praised Allah with, bring it; and what you praised me with, leave it. So I began to recite to him. Then a tall, aquiline-nosed man entered, and he said to me: Stop. When he went out, he said: Bring it. So I began to recite to him. Before long he returned, and he said to me: Stop. When he went out, he said: Bring it. I said: Who is this, O Prophet of Allah, that when he enters you say: Stop, and when he goes out you say: Bring it? He said: This is Umar ibn al-Khattab, and there is nothing of falsehood in him."
"846","Aswad ibn Zayd al-Ansari, a veteran of Badr. Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Helpers, then from al-Khazraj of Banu Salimah: Aswad ibn Zayd ibn Tha'labah ibn Ghanm."
"847","Ayman ibn Umm Ayman, martyred on the day of Hunayn - he is Ayman ibn Ubayd, of Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj; he is the maternal brother of Usamah ibn Zayd. Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Hunayn: Ayman ibn Ubayd."
"848","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Zakariyya, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, who said: Sa'd said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw Ayman fleeing from battle, and I recognized displeasure on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sa'd said: I said: I have not seen a sermon further from every good. Then they faced battle after that, and Sa'd said: I saw Ayman plunging into the thick of the people, and that pleased the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Ayman: I have been told that you do not stand between the two ranks out of cowardice. He said: I hope to stand a stand that Allah and His Messenger love. Umar said: You are indeed fit to do so."
"849","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Zakariyya, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, who said: Ayman was in charge of the purification water of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his sandals, and would hand him what he needed."
"850","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid and Ata, from Ayman al-Habashi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The least for which the thief's hand is cut is the price of a shield. He said: And it used to be valued at a dinar."
"851","Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Abu Awanah, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Ata, from Ayman al-Habashi, who said: Hands were cut in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the price of a shield."
"852","Ayman ibn Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi. Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Mutarrif - then I met Mutarrif and he narrated to me - from al-Sha'bi, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan said to Ayman ibn Khuraym: Will you not fight with us? He said: My father and my uncle witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they ordered me not to fight. Then he recited verse saying: Jurmi jurm..."
"853","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Aban narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir al-Sha'bi, who said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam was fighting al-Dahhak ibn Qays, and he said to a man of Banu Asad called Ayman ibn Khuraym: Will you not fight with us? He said: No; my father and my uncle witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they enjoined upon me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but Allah. If you bring me a clearance from the Fire, I will fight with you. He said: Go, we have no need of you. Ayman said: ..."
"854","Chapter: Those named Umayyah. Umayyah ibn Lawdhan al-Ansari, a veteran of Badr. Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Helpers, then from Banu Qarbus ibn Ghanm ibn Salim: Umayyah ibn Lawdhan ibn Salim ibn Thabit ibn Hazzal ibn Amr ibn Qarbus ibn Ghanm."
"855","Umayyah ibn Makhshi al-Khuza'i. Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Jabir ibn Subayh narrated to me: al-Muthanna ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khuza'i narrated to me - and I accompanied him to Wasit; whenever he ate, he would mention Allah's name, and when he came to the last morsel, he would say: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end. I said to him about that, and he said: My grandfather Umayyah ibn Makhshi narrated to me - and he was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that a man used to eat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not mention Allah's name. When he came to the last morsel, he said: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan kept eating with him until he said: at its beginning and its end; then Satan vomited up all that he had eaten."
"856","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Raja ibn Subh narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his uncle Umayyah ibn Makhshi - who was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, and a man was eating and did not mention Allah's name until only a morsel of his food remained. He said: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then said: Satan kept eating with you, and when you mentioned the name of Allah, he vomited up what was in his belly."
"857","Umayyah ibn Amr al-Damri al-Kinani. Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Raja'i narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi' narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri informed me, from his father, from his grandfather: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him as a scout to Quraysh. I came to the wooden scaffold of Khubayb while fearing the watchers. I climbed it and untied him, and he fell to the ground. I stopped not far away, then I looked and did not see the scaffold of Khubayb - as though the earth had swallowed it. No trace of Khubayb was mentioned until this hour."
"858","Umayyah ibn Khalid ibn Asid ibn Abi al-Is ibn Umayyah. Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek victory through the poor Emigrants."
"859","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Umayyah ibn Khalid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek victory through the poor Emigrants."
"860","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us: Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from Umayyah ibn Khalid, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek victory - seek help - through the poor Muslims."
"861","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, who said: Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid led us in prayer in Khurasan and recited these two surahs: We seek Your help and we seek Your forgiveness - and he mentioned the hadith."
"862","Awfa ibn Mawalah al-Anazi. Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah and Ahmad ibn Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Munqidh ibn Husayn ibn Jahwan ibn Abi Awfa ibn Mawalah al-Anazi narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Awfa ibn Mawalah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he granted me al-Ghamim and stipulated upon me: the wayfarer is the first to drink his fill. And he granted Sa'idah - a man of us - a well in the desert called al-Ja'uniyyah, a well in which water is stored, not sweet water. And he granted Iyas ibn Qatadah al-Anazi al-Jabiyah, which is short of Yamamah. We had all come to him together, and he wrote for each of us to that effect on leather."
"863","Uhban ibn Sayfi al-Ghifari, who died in Basra. Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Udaysah bint Uhban, who said: When death came to my father, he said: Do not shroud me in a sewn garment. When he passed away and was washed, they sent to me: Send the shroud. So I sent them the shroud. They said: A shirt. I said: My father forbade me to shroud him in a sewn shirt. I had sent to the fuller, and my father had a shirt with the fuller; it was brought and he was dressed in it and taken away. I closed my door and followed him, then returned, and the shirt was in the house. I sent to those who had washed my father and said: Did you shroud him in a shirt? They said: Yes. I said: Is it this one? They said: Yes."
"864","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ubayd narrated to me, from Udaysah bint Uhban ibn Sayfi, who said: When Ali ibn Abi Talib came to Basra, he came to my father and stood at the door and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: Will you not come out and help me against these people? He said: Yes, if you wish. O slave girl, hand me the sword. She handed him the sword and he placed it in his lap, then drew it. He said: Your close friend and your cousin (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, when there is fighting between two tribes of Muslims, to take a sword of wood. He drew part of it while it was in his lap and said: If you wish, I will come out with you with this. He said: I have no need of you."
"865","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Qasmali, from the daughter of Uhban: Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Uhban and said: What prevents you from following me? He said: My close friend - meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - advised me, saying: There will be trial and division; when that happens, break your sword and take a sword of wood. And he ordered his family, when he became gravely ill, to shroud him and not dress him in a shirt. So we dressed him in a shirt, and in the morning the shirt was on the clothes-rack."
"866","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rustum, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd, from Udaysah bint Uhban ibn Sayfi al-Ghifari, from her father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you see two men of my community fighting over wealth, prepare at that time a sword of wood."
"867","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ubayd, the muezzin of the mosque of Jaradan, narrated to us, from Udaysah bint Uhban ibn Sayfi, who said: When Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Basra, he came to us at the house and said: Is Abu Muslim here? We said: Yes. He came out to him, and Ali said to him: Will you not help us in this matter? He said: Yes. O slave girl, bring me that sword. She brought his sword and he drew it, and it was a sword of wood. Abu Muslim said to him: Your cousin - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - enjoined upon me: when there is trial among the Muslims, to take a sword of wood. Ali turned away angry and said: We have no need of you nor of your sword. Yazid ibn Zuray' said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated this hadith to me from this shaykh before I met him."
"868","Al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Kabir al-Ghifari, who said: Udaysah bint Uhban ibn Sayfi narrated to me: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came to her father, stood at the door, sought permission, and said: O Abu Muslim, what prevents you from striving in this matter and taking your share of it? He said: What prevents me is a covenant my close friend and your cousin (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made with me: he commanded me, when trial falls, to take a sword of wood. Here it is with me; if you wish, I will fight with it."
"869","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih al-Basri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Zahdam ibn al-Harith al-Ghifari narrated to us: my father narrated to me, saying: Uhban ibn Sayfi said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Uhban, if you remain after me, you will see disagreement among my Companions. If you live until that day, make your sword of palm stalks. He said: So I made my sword of palm stalks. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came to me, took hold of the two doorposts, then greeted and said: O Uhban, will you not come out? I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Abu al-Hasan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me - or commanded me - or advised me - or charged me - Ibn Zahdam doubted - saying: O Uhban, if you remain after me, you will see disagreement among my Companions; if you live until that day, make your sword of palm stalks. So I brought out my sword to him, and Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) turned away."
"870","Asma' ibn Harithah al-Aslami. Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi narrated to us; and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Wahb narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hind ibn Harithah narrated to me, from his uncle Asma' ibn Harithah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on the day of Ashura and said: Go to your people and order them to fast this day. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not think I will reach them before they eat. He said: Order whoever of them has eaten to fast the rest of his day."
"871","870 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated, al-Haytham ibn Adi narrated, your father Ghaylan ibn Abd Allah narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Asma ibn Harithah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his hand, I think on his thigh, pointing with his finger during the tashahhud."
"872","871 - And with its chain, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turning to his left toward his house when he gave the salutation."
"873","76 - Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn. 872 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ali al-Ansari narrated, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab, from Abu Nahik, from Shibl ibn Khulayd al-Muzani, from Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so rushes in battle? He said: He is in the Fire. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so, with his worship, striving and gentleness, is in the Fire, then where are we? He said: That is only the submission of hypocrisy, and he is in the Fire. He said: We watched him in battle; no horseman or foot soldier passed by him except he leapt upon him, so his wounds became many. We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has been martyred. He said: He is in the Fire. When the pain of the wounds became severe upon him, he took his sword and placed it between his breasts, then leaned upon it until it came out of his back. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise while he is among the people of the Fire, and a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire while he is among the people of Paradise; misery or felicity overtakes him at the departure of his soul, and he is sealed with it."
"874","77 - Udhaynah Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Laythi, and he is Udhaynah ibn al-Harith ibn Ya'mur ibn Awf ibn Ka'b ibn Amir ibn Layth. 873 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asbahani narrated, (H) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi, Sa'id ibn Mansur and Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath then sees something else better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath."
"875","78 - Asram. 874 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, Bashir ibn Maymun narrated, from Usamah ibn Akhdari, from Asram, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought a slave, so supplicate to Allah for blessing for him and name him. He said: What is your name? He said: Asram. He said: Rather you are Zur'ah. He said: What do you want for him? He said: Zarra'an. He said: Then he is Asim."
"876","79 - al-Asla' ibn Sharik al-Ashja'i. 875 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, (H) and Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, they both said: al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated, my father narrated to me, from his father, from a man of us called al-Asla', he said: I used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saddle his mount. One night he said to me: O Asla', get up and saddle. I said: O Messenger of Allah, major impurity has befallen me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent, then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him with the verse of the earth-surface, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Get up, O Asla', and perform tayammum. He said: So I got up and performed tayammum, then saddled for him. He traveled until he passed by water, and said to me: O Asla', touch - or make touch - this skin of yours. He said: And my father showed me the tayammum as his father showed him: one strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows."
"877","876 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Asla', a man of Banu al-A'raj ibn Ka'b, he said: I used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: O Asla', get up, show me how such-and-such? I said: O Messenger of Allah, major impurity has befallen me. He fell silent for a while until Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him with the earth-surface, the tayammum. He said: Get up, O Asla', and perform tayammum. He said: Then al-Asla' showed me how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him tayammum. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the earth with his palms, shook them off, wiped his face with them until he passed over his beard, returned them to the earth, wiped his palms on the earth, rubbed one against the other, shook them off, then wiped his forearms, their outer and inner sides."
"878","877 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated, al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Suwiyyah al-Minqari narrated, al-Haytham ibn Ruzayq al-Maliki of Banu Malik ibn Ka'b ibn Sa'd, who lived one hundred and seventeen years, narrated, from his father, from al-Asla' ibn Sharik, he said: I used to saddle the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Major impurity befell me on a cold night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to depart. I disliked saddling his camel while in a state of major impurity, and feared that washing with cold water would kill me or make me ill. So I ordered a man of the Ansar and he saddled it, and I placed stones and heated water with them and washed. Then I caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. He said: O Asla', why do I see your saddling changed? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not saddle it; a man of the Ansar saddled it. He said: Why? I said: Major impurity befell me and I feared the cold for myself, so I ordered him to saddle it, placed stones, heated water and washed with it. Then Allah sent down: O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated, up to: Indeed Allah is Pardoning, Forgiving."
"879","80 - al-Aqra' ibn Habis al-Tamimi al-Mujashi'i. 878 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Wahb narrated, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Aqra' ibn Habis, that he called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind the chambers and said: O Muhammad, my praise is an adornment and my blame is a disgrace. He said: That is Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"880","81 - al-Agharr al-Muzani. 879 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Nafi', that Ibn Umar informed him, that al-Agharr, a man of Muzaynah who had companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was owed wasqs of dates by a man of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and he went to him repeatedly. He said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) with me. He said: Everyone we met greeted us, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do you not see the people beginning you with greeting so they get the reward? Begin them with greeting so you get the reward."
"881","880 - Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi narrated, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from al-Agharr, Agharr Muzaynah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had assigned me a portion of dates held by a man of the Ansar, and he delayed me. I spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Go with him in the morning, O Abu Bakr, and take his dates for him. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) promised me at the mosque when we prayed dawn; I found him where he promised me, and we set out. Whenever a man saw Abu Bakr from afar, he greeted him. Abu Bakr said: Do you not see what excellence the people gain over you? Let no one precede you in greeting. Whenever a man appeared, we hastened to greet him before he greeted us."
"882","881 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Shabib Abu Rawh, from al-Agharr, among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recited the chapter of al-Rum."
"883","882 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Burdah narrating, from al-Agharr, who was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard the Prophet say: I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times a day."
"884","883 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated, Mis'ar narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, repent to your Lord; by Allah, I repent to my Lord one hundred times a day."
"885","884 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Ali narrated, from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"886","885 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, he said: I sat with a man of the Emigrants, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day."
"887","886 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated, Mu'tamir narrated, he said: I heard Ayyub narrating, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from a man of the Emigrants, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, for I seek forgiveness and repent to Him in a day - or every day - one hundred times, or more than once."
"888","887 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, (H) and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Isa ibn Shadhan narrated, Dawud ibn Shabib narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My heart is clouded until I seek forgiveness one hundred times a day."
"889","888 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, (H) and al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr al-Muzani, who had companionship, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My heart is clouded, and I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times every day."
"890","889 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Bahr al-Bayrudhi narrated, Awn ibn Umarah narrated, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My heart is clouded and I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times."
"891","890 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi say: I asked Abu Ubaydah Ma'mar ibn al-Muthanna about the interpretation of his saying: My heart is clouded, and he did not interpret it for me; and I asked al-Asma'i about it and he did not interpret it."
"892","891 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Khalid ibn Abi Karimah narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to us, from al-Agharr al-Muzani, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, morning came upon me and I have not performed witr. He said: Witr is only at night. He said: O Prophet of Allah, morning came upon me and I have not performed witr. He said: Then perform witr."
"893","82 - As'ad ibn Harithah ibn Lawdhan al-Ansari. 892 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of the Bridge among the Ansar, then of Banu Sa'idah: As'ad ibn Harithah ibn Lawdhan."
"894","84 - As'ad ibn Zayd al-Ansari, a Badri. 893 - al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr among the Ansar, then of Banu Zurayq: As'ad ibn Zayd ibn al-Fakih ibn Zayd ibn Khaldah ibn Amir ibn Ajlan."
"895","84 - As'ad ibn Zurarah al-Ansari of Banu al-Najjar, kunya Abu Umamah; he died in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the first year of the Hijrah. 894 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated that to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated, Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated, Ibn Ishaq narrated, and Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: In the first year Abu Umamah As'ad ibn Zurarah perished; quinsy seized him while the mosque was being built."
"896","895 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated, Waki' narrated, from Zam'ah ibn Salih, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that As'ad ibn Zurarah was one of the naqibs on the night of al-Aqabah."
"897","896 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn As'ad ibn Zurarah, our uncle narrated to us, that Abu Umamah was struck by a pain which the people of Madinah call dhibh (throat disease). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely do my utmost - or convey my excuse - regarding Abu Umamah. He said: So he cauterized him with his hand and he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An evil death for the Jews to say: Why was it not lifted from his companion; and I control nothing for him nor for myself from Allah."
"898","897 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who attended al-Aqabah among the Ansar, then of Banu al-Najjar: Abu Umamah As'ad ibn Zurarah, and he was a naqib."
"899","898 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shu'aythi narrated, from Zufar ibn Wathimah al-Nasri, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that As'ad ibn Zurarah said to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to al-Dahhak ibn Qays that he should give the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi inheritance from her husband's blood-money."
"900","899 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Rajjani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated, Asim ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me, from As'ad ibn Zurarah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that Allah shade him on a day when there is no shade but His shade, let him ease a debtor or remit from him."
"901","900 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to me, from his father, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: I used to lead my father when his sight was gone; whenever I took him out to Friday prayer he sought forgiveness for Abu Umamah As'ad ibn Zurarah. I said: O my father, what about your seeking forgiveness for As'ad ibn Zurarah whenever you hear the call on Friday? He said: O my son, As'ad was the first to gather us for Friday in Madinah before the arrival of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in Hazm of the Harrah of Banu Bayadah, in Naqi' al-Hadamat. I said: How many were you then? He said: Forty men."
"902","85 - As'ad ibn Salamah al-Ansari. 901 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those martyred on the Day of Yamamah among the Ansar, then of Banu Abd al-Ashhal: As'ad ibn Salamah."
"903","As'ad ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf Abu Umamah; he has vision (of the Prophet). 902 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf died in the year one hundred."
"904","903 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Bakkar al-Sa'di narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: The first to pray Duha was a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) known as Abu al-Zawa'id."
"905","Chapter of the one named Aqram, one person. 87 - Aqram Abu Abd Allah al-Khuza'i. 904 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Abu al-Muthanna Sulayman ibn Yazid al-Ka'bi narrated, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Ibn Aqram, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I was grazing sheep at al-Qa' of Namirah when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alight there; he established the prayer and prayed with his companions, and I prayed with them, as if I see the whiteness of what is beneath the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while prostrating."
"906","88 - al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam al-Makhzumi, a Badri. 905 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr of Quraysh, then of Banu Makhzum ibn Nuqtah ibn Murrah ibn Ka'b: al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam; and the name of Abu al-Arqam is Abd Manaf, kunya Abu Khindif ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Makhzum."
"907","906 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr: al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam."
"908","907 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, Attaf ibn Khalid narrated, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, from his grandfather al-Arqam, who was a Badri; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sheltered in his house at al-Safa until they reached forty Muslim men, the last of them to embrace Islam being Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him); when they were forty they went out to the polytheists. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to bid him farewell, intending to go out to Bayt al-Maqdis. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Where are you going? I said: I want Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: What takes you there, is it trade? I said: No, but I pray in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer here is better than a thousand prayers there."
"909","908 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dinbaji al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated, from Hisham ibn Ziyad, from Ammar ibn Sa'd, from Uthman ibn Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam al-Makhzumi, from his father al-Arqam, who was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who steps over people's necks on Friday and separates between them is like one dragging his intestines in the Fire."
"910","909 - Ahmad ibn al-Ja'd al-Washsha narrated to us, Abu Mus'ab narrated, Yahya ibn Imran narrated, from his grandfather Uthman ibn al-Arqam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the Day of Badr: Lay down whatever spoils you have with you."
"911","Chapter of those named Ibrahim. 89 - Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibrahim; and it is said his name is Aslam. 910 - Muhammad ibn Ali Fustuqah narrated to us, Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated, he said: Aslam, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died after the killing of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) in the year thirty-five."
"912","911 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Numayr narrated, a man of the people of Madinah narrated to me, that the name of Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is Aslam."
"913","What Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from Abu Rafi'. 912 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq say: Husayn ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was a boy belonging to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib; I had embraced Islam, Umm al-Fadl had embraced Islam, and al-Abbas had embraced Islam, but he concealed his Islam fearing his people. Abu Lahab had stayed behind from Badr and sent al-As ibn Hisham in his place, to whom he owed a debt, saying to him: Spare me this expedition and I will leave you what you owe me; so he did. When the news came and Allah humiliated Abu Lahab, and I was a weak man carving these cups in a chamber, he passed by me - by Allah, I was sitting in the chamber carving my cups with Umm al-Fadl beside me, when the evildoer Abu Lahab came dragging his feet - I think he said: until he sat at the tent-rope of the chamber - his back to my back. The people said: This is Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith. Abu Lahab said: Come to me, O son of my brother. Abu Sufyan came and sat beside him, and the people gathered over them. He said: O son of my brother, how was the affair of the people? He said: Nothing; by Allah, no sooner did we meet them than we gave them our shoulders, they killing us as they pleased and capturing us as they pleased; and by Allah, I do not blame the people. He said: Why? He said: I saw white men on piebald horses; by Allah, they left nothing untouched and nothing could stand against them. He said: So I lifted the tent-rope of the chamber and said: By Allah, those were the angels. Abu Lahab raised his hand and struck my face; I grappled with him, he lifted me and threw me to the ground and got on top of me. Umm al-Fadl stood up, girded herself, took a post from the posts of the chamber and struck him with it, splitting an ugly wound in his head, saying: O enemy of Allah, you deemed him weak because you saw his master absent from him. He stood up humiliated; by Allah, he lived only seven nights until Allah struck him with the lentil-disease and killed him. His two sons left him two or three nights without burying him until he stank. A man of Quraysh said to his two sons: Are you not ashamed? Your father has stunk in his house? They said: We fear this ulcer, and Quraysh used to fear the lentil-disease as the plague is feared. A man said: Go, and I am with you. He said: By Allah, they washed him only by throwing water upon him from afar, then carried him and threw him in upper Makkah against a wall, and threw stones upon him."
"914","Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Rafi'. 913 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Malik informed me, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a young camel; then charity camels came to him. Abu Rafi' said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to repay the man his young camel. I stood up and found among the camels only choice full-grown camels in their sixth year. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it to him, for the best of the Muslims are the best in repayment."
"915","914 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a young camel from a man, saying: When charity comes we shall repay you. When charity came, he said to Abu Rafi': Repay this man his young camel. He looked among them and found only a full-grown camel in its sixth year or older. He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Give him, for the best of people are the best in repayment."
"916","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Rafi'. 915 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym and Arim narrated, (H) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, (H) and Yusuf the judge and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, (H) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Matar al-Warraq, Rabi'ah narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in a state of halal, and consummated with her while in halal, and I was the messenger between them."
"917","916 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated, that he heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not order me to alight there - meaning al-Abtah - but I pitched his dome and he came and alighted. Sufyan said: Amr ibn Dinar used to narrate this hadith from Salih ibn Kaysan; when he came to us, Amr ibn Dinar said to us: Go to this one and ask him about this hadith."
"918","Ali ibn al-Husayn from Abu Rafi'. 917 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated, they said: Sharik narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Abu Rafi', he said: When Fatimah gave birth to Hasan (may Allah be pleased with them both), she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not offer an aqiqah for my son? He said: No, but shave his head and give charity with the weight of his hair in wariq - or he said: silver - to the poor. When she gave birth to Husayn she did the same with him; and Musa ibn Dawud said in his hadith: to the Awfad and the poor."
"919","918 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated, Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that when Fatimah gave birth to al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), she wanted to offer an aqiqah for him with a great ram. She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not offer any aqiqah for him; but shave the hair of his head, then give charity with its weight in silver in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to the Awfad. Then she gave birth to al-Husayn ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) the next year and did the same with him."
"920","919 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards what is between his two jawbones and his thighs shall enter Paradise."
"921","920 - Abdan and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated, Sa'id ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed, he bought two fat horned black-and-white rams; when he had addressed the people and prayed, one of them was brought while he was standing in his prayer place, and he slaughtered it himself with the knife, then said: This is for my entire ummah, whoever bore witness to You of tawhid and bore witness to me of conveyance. Then the other was brought and he slaughtered it himself, then said: O Allah, this is for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad. He gave them both entirely to the poor, and he and his family ate from them both."
"922","921 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, (H) and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, they said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn Husayn, that Abu Rafi' narrated to him, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed, two fat horned black-and-white rams due for sacrifice were brought; when he had addressed the people, given salutation and finished, one of them was brought while he was standing in his prayer place, and he slaughtered it himself, then said: O Allah, this is for my ummah, whoever bore witness to You of tawhid and to me of conveyance. Then the other was brought and he slaughtered it himself, then said: O Allah, this is for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad. He and his family ate from them both and fed both entirely to the poor. We remained years with no man of Banu Hashim sacrificing; Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, had sufficed them the burden through the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"923","922 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sacrifice, he bought two horned black-and-white rams; when he had prayed and addressed, he called for one of them while in his prayer place and slaughtered it, then said: O Allah, this is for my entire ummah, whoever bore witness to You of tawhid and bore witness to me of conveyance. Then he brought the other and slaughtered it, then said: O Allah, this is for Muhammad and his household."
"924","923 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two black-and-white horned rams."
"925","924 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Sharik narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that when the caller to prayer called, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say as he says; when he said: Come to prayer, he said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"926","925 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mayfa' ibn al-Sabbah al-Hamdani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that no religion in Madinah other than Islam be left except it be expelled."
"927","926 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the adhan in the ears of al-Hasan and al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) when they were born, and ordered it; and the wording is al-Himmani's."
"928","Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar from Abu Rafi'. 927 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, (H) and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, they said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad ibn Tahla narrated, from Abu al-Rijal, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to kill dogs. I went out killing every one I met until I came to al-Usayyah; there was a dog around a house, and I aimed at it to kill it. A woman from the house called to me: What do you want? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to kill dogs. She said: Return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him that I am a woman whose sight is gone; it announces visitors to me and drives wild beasts from me. I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return and kill it. So I returned and killed it."
"929","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Abu Rafi'. 928 - Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Ali al-Harrani narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Harrani narrated, they said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Shaybah ibn Nisah, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, from Abu Rafi', he said: A writing reached me containing the opening supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he said takbir he would say: I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, a Hanif, and I am not among the polytheists. My prayer, my rites, my life and my death are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, with no partner to Him; with that I am commanded and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You, glory be to You and with Your praise; You are my Lord and I am Your servant, no partner to You; I wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins, for none forgives sins but You. At Your service and aided by You, all good is in Your hands; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. Then he would recite."
"930","Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi from Abu Rafi'. 929 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Basri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, he said: I heard Abu Rafi' say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person and conceals it, forty major sins are forgiven him; and whoever digs a grave for his brother until he shelters him in it, it is as if he housed him in a dwelling once until he is resurrected."
"931","Yazid ibn Ziyad, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him). 930 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, guide a man through your hands is better for you than all upon which the sun has risen and set."
"932","Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi' from his father. 931 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call the adhan with the prayer in the ear of al-Hasan ibn Ali when Fatimah gave birth to him (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"933","932 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, who was the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of Banu Makhzum over charity. He said: Accompany me so you may get some of it. I said: Until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came to him and asked him. He said: The freedman of a people is of themselves, and charity is not lawful for us."
"934","933 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of Banu Makhzum over charity. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity in less than five wasqs, no charity in less than five camels, and no charity in less than five uqiyyahs."
"935","934 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated, (H). And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, they said: Sufyan narrated, Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let me not find one of you reclining on his couch when there comes to him a matter of what I commanded or forbade, saying: We do not know; whatever we found in the Book of Allah we followed."
"936","935 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Sufyan narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"937","936 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salim al-Makki, from Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays, from Ubayd Allah ibn Qays, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"938","937 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: al-Qa'nabi narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution three times three times; al-Qa'nabi added in his hadith: and twice and once."
"939","938 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Fazari al-Kufi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us bright of color, joy recognized in his face, and said: I saw my Lord in the finest form. He said to me: O Muhammad, do you know concerning what the highest assembly disputes? I said: O Lord, concerning expiations. He said: And what are the expiations? I said: Conveying ablution to its places despite dislikes, walking on foot to prayers, and awaiting prayer after prayer."
"940","939 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, (H). And Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi narrated to us, Luwayn narrated, they said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to apply ithmid kohl while fasting."
"941","940 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a scorpion while praying."
"942","941 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated, Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: When Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) killed the standard-bearers on the Day of Uhud, Jibril (peace be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, this is true solidarity. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is of me and I am of him. Jibril said: And I am of you both, O Messenger of Allah."
"943","942 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Mondays and Thursdays."
"944","943 - And with its chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out to the two Eids walking, pray without adhan or iqamah, then return walking by another road."
"945","944 - And with its chain, he said: We slaughtered a young she-goat for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he ate and did not perform ablution, did not touch water, and did not rinse his mouth."
"946","945 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sharp-edged stone and roasted it; he ate and did not rinse his mouth nor perform ablution."
"947","946 - Ahmad ibn al-Abbas al-Murri al-Qantari narrated to us, Harb ibn al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali on an expedition; when he returned, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah, His Messenger and Jibril, upon them be peace, are pleased with you."
"948","947 - And with its chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Whoever loves him has loved me, and whoever loves me, Allah has loved him; and whoever hates him has hated me, and whoever hates me has hated Allah."
"949","948 - And with its chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You and your partisans shall come to me at the Basin well-watered and quenched, your faces whitened; and your enemy shall come to me thirsty and disfigured."
"950","949 - And with its chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased that you are my brother and I am your brother?"
"951","950 - And with its chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: The first four to enter Paradise are I and you, al-Hasan and al-Husayn; our descendants behind our backs, our wives behind our descendants, and our partisans to our right and our left."
"952","951 - And with its chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: By the One in whose hand is my soul, were it not that groups of my ummah would say about you what the Christians said about Isa son of Maryam, I would say about you today a saying such that no Muslim you pass by would fail to take dust from the traces of your feet seeking blessing through it."
"953","952 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ali ibn Hashim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on Monday morning, Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) prayed on Monday at the end of the day, and Ali prayed on Tuesday. Ali remained praying secretly seven years and months before anyone prayed."
"954","953 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a place and said: What an excellent bathhouse place this is; so a bathhouse was built in it."
"955","954 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Ali ibn Hashim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar ibn Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him): The transgressing party shall kill you."
"956","955 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat narrated, Ali ibn Hashim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rafi' narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Rafi', he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sleeping or being inspired, and there was a snake at the side of the house. I disliked killing it lest I wake him, so I lay down between him and the snake; if anything happened it would be to me before him. He awoke reciting this verse: Your ally is only Allah, His Messenger and those who believe, the verse. He said: Praise be to Allah. He saw me beside him and said: What laid you here? I said: Because of this snake. He said: Get up to it and kill it. So I killed it, and he praised Allah. Then he took my hand and said: O Abu Rafi', after me there shall be a people who fight Ali; jihad against them is a duty upon Allah. Whoever cannot wage jihad against them with his hand, then with his tongue; whoever cannot with his tongue, then with his heart; there is nothing beyond that."
"957","956 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Harmalah al-Abdi narrated, Ibrahim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Rafi', that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed his ablution for prayer, he moved his ring on his finger."
"958","957 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, al-Mu'tamir ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a ram, then said: This is for me and for my ummah."
"959","958 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his brother Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of your ears rings, let him remember me, send blessings upon me, and say: May Allah mention with good whoever mentioned me."
"960","Al-Mughirah ibn Abi Rafi' from his father. 959 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, al-Mughirah ibn Abi Rafi' informed me, from Abu Rafi', that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a sheep's shoulder, then pray without touching water."
"961","960 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought a shoulder; he ate it, then prayed without touching a drop of water."
"962","Salih ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi' from his grandfather. 961 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim ibn Jabr narrated to me, from Rabah ibn Salih ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the depth of night supplicating at al-Baqi', with Abu Rafi' beside him. He supplicated whatever Allah willed, then turned back; he passed by a grave and said: Uff, uff, uff. Abu Rafi' said to him: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, there is no one with you but me - was it at me you said uff? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but I said uff at the occupant of this grave, who was asked about me and doubted concerning me."
"963","Al-Fadl ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi'. 962 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Ibn Jurayj, Manbudh, a man of the family of Abu Rafi', narrated to me, from al-Fadl ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr he would sometimes go to Banu Abd al-Ashhal and converse with them, sometimes conversing until Maghrib prayer. Once while I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Maghrib prayer, he hurrying, we passed by al-Baqi'. He said: Uff, uff to you. I thought he meant me, so he said to me: Walk on, what is with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, have I done something new? He said: What is that? I said: You said uff at me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but this is the grave of so-and-so; I sent him as a collector over Banu so-and-so, and he misappropriated a coat of mail, so now one like it of Fire has been put upon him."
"964","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' from his grandfather. 963 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, (H). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him, that al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to him, that Abu Rafi' informed him, that he came with a letter from Quraysh to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Islam was cast into my heart. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I shall never return to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not betray a covenant nor detain envoys; but return, and if what is in your heart now remains, then come back. So I returned to them, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and embraced Islam."
"965","964 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr narrated to him, that al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to him, that Abu Rafi' informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. I said: O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you handed me, you would have kept handing me."
"966","965 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' it was narrated to him, that Abu Rafi' narrated to him, that he is the man of the foreleg. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. I said: O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you handed me, you would have kept handing me."
"967","Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' from his grandfather. 966 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, Fayid, freedman of Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, from his grandfather, he said: A sheep's belly was cooked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he ate from it, then prayed Isha without performing ablution."
"968","967 - And with its chain, he said: I slaughtered a sheep with a peg. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered a sheep with a peg. He said: Eat it."
"969","968 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibn al-Had, from Abadil ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from Abu Rafi', he said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking in Baqi' al-Gharqad with me walking behind him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not be guided, may you not be guided, three times. Abu Rafi' said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with me? He said: I do not mean you; I mean the occupant of this grave - he is asked about me and claims he does not know me. It was a grave upon which water had been sprinkled when its occupant was buried."
"970","969 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Fa'id, freedman of Abadil, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to roast a sheep for him. I roasted it for him. He said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many forelegs does it have? He said: Had you remained silent, you would have found one as long as I called you."
"971","Salma, mother of the sons of Rafi', from Abu Rafi'. 970 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', from his aunt Salma, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us while we had a cooked sheep. He said: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him and he ate it. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him and he ate it. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. I said: O Messenger of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you remained silent, you would have given me forelegs as long as I called for them."
"972","971 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Aban ibn Salih, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Salma, from Abu Rafi', he said: People came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us of this community which you ordered to be killed - meaning dogs? So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent down: They ask you what is lawful for them, the verse."
"973","972 - And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, they said: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated, Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Salma Umm Rafi', from Abu Rafi', he said: Jibril came seeking permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He gave him permission, but he was slow upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his cloak and stood up to him while he was standing at the door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given permission. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but we do not enter a house containing a dog or an image. They found a puppy in one of their houses. Abu Rafi' said: When morning came he ordered me, and I left no dog in Madinah except I killed it. Then there was a distant woman with a dog barking for her; I pitied her and left it, and came. He ordered me, so I returned to the dog and killed it. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us of this community which you ordered to be killed? So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent down: They ask you what is lawful for them; say: Lawful for you are the good things."
"974","973 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf the judge narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H) and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', from his aunt Salma, from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around all his wives together, washing at each one of them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you not make it one washing? He said: This is purer and better."
"975","974 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, from Ibn al-Had, from Abadil, from his grandmother, the wife of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', he said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Baqi' al-Gharqad walking behind him, he said: May you not be guided, may you not be guided. Abu Rafi' said: I turned but saw no one. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is my affair? He said: I do not mean you, but I mean the occupant of the grave; he is asked about me and claims he does not know me. It was a grave sprinkled upon when its occupant was buried."
"976","Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays from Abu Rafi'. 975 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while people were around him: Let me not recognize one of you to whom there comes a matter of my affair while reclining on his couch, saying: Whatever we found in the Book of Allah we acted upon."
"977","Amr ibn al-Sharid from Abu Rafi'. 976 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor is most entitled to his adjoining property."
"978","977 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, (H) and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, (H) and Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, they said: Sufyan narrated, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated, he said: I heard Amr ibn al-Sharid say: al-Miswar ibn Makhramah took my hand and said: Let us go to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. I went out with him, his hand upon one of my shoulders. Abu Rafi' came and said to al-Miswar: Will you not order this one - meaning Sa'd - to buy from me my two houses in his dwelling? Sa'd said: By Allah, I shall not give you more than four hundred dinars - either he said: in installments, or he said: deferred. Abu Rafi' said: By Allah, I could have sold them for five hundred dinars cash; were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The neighbor is most entitled to his adjoining property, I would not have sold to you. And the wording is al-Humaydi's."
"979","978 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from Abu Rafi', he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The neighbor is most entitled to his adjoining property."
"980","Abu Ghatfan ibn Tarif al-Murri from Abu Rafi'. 979 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Batik narrated, from Abadil ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', from Umar ibn Aban, from Abu Ghatfan ibn Tarif al-Murri, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he roasted meat for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"981","980 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Abadil of the descendants of Abu Rafi', from Abu Ghatfan ibn Tarif al-Murri, from Abu Rafi', he said: I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he ordered me and I made for him from its bellies, and he ate from it, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"982","981 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, (H) and Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Ghatfan, from Abu Rafi', he said: I bear witness - I used to roast the sheep's belly for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would eat from it, then pray without performing ablution."
"983","Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Abu Rafi'. 982 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate of sheep meat without performing ablution."
"984","Shurahbil ibn Sa'd from Abu Rafi'. 983 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Ali narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd, from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat, then prayed without performing ablution."
"985","984 - Isma'il ibn Thumayl al-Khallal al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I roasted a sheep's belly for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"986","985 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abd Allah ibn Aradah narrated, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd, from Abu Rafi', he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by a pot of one of his household in which meat was cooking; one of them handed him a shoulder from it, and he ate it standing, then prayed without performing ablution."
"987","986 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'afa al-Harrani narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Shurahbil ibn Sa'd, from Abu Rafi', he said: A sheep was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I roasted some of it, he ate from it, then stood and prayed without touching water."
"988","Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Abu Rafi'. 987 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas: O uncle, shall I not join you, shall I not gift you, shall I not benefit you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Pray, O uncle, four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah the Opening of the Book and a chapter; when the recitation ends, say: Allah is Greatest, praise be to Allah, glory be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, fifteen times before bowing. Then bow and say it ten times, raise your head and say it ten times, prostrate and say it ten times, raise your head and say it ten times, prostrate and say it ten times, raise your head and say it ten times, then stand - that is seventy-five in each rak'ah, three hundred in four rak'ahs. Even if your sins were like the foam of the sea, Allah would forgive you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, who can say it every day? He said: If you cannot pray it in a day, pray it in a Friday, until he said: Pray it in a month, until he said: Pray it in a year."
"989","Al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab from Abu Rafi'. 988 - al-Muqaddam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib, from Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Baqi' and said: Uff, uff, uff, with no one beside me but me. It startled me, and I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: The occupant of this pit - I employed him over Banu so-and-so, and he betrayed a cloak; I was shown it blazing upon him."
"990","Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt from Abu Rafi'. 989 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hosted a guest but found nothing with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to serve him. He sent to a Jewish man saying: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to you: Lend me flour until the crescent of Rajab. He said: Only with a pledge. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Nay, by Allah, I am trustworthy in heaven, trustworthy on earth; had he lent me or sold to me I would have repaid him. When I left him, this verse was sent down: And do not extend your eyes to what We have granted enjoyment to spouses among them, to the end of the verse, for He consoles him about the world."
"991","Abu Sa'id al-Ta'ifi from Abu Rafi'. 990 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, from a man, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to pray with his head tied up."
"992","991 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Mukhawwal, from Abu Sa'id, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was prostrating with my hair tied; he untied it and forbade me from that."
"993","992 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, he said: An elder of the people of Ta'if known as Abu Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Rafi', that he saw al-Husayn ibn Ali prostrating with his hair tied; Abu Rafi' said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you shall pray while tying up his hair."
"994","993 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Imran ibn Musa informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, that he saw Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pass by Husayn ibn Ali while Husayn was praying standing with his braid tucked into the back of his neck; Abu Rafi' untied it, and Husayn turned angrily. Abu Rafi' said: Attend to your prayer and do not be angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: That is the share of Satan - he says: the seat of Satan - meaning the tucking of his braid."
"995","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, freedman of Ali, from Abu Rafi'. 994 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn the judge and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, freedman of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), from Abu Rafi', he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali to Yemen and tied a banner for him; when he set out he said: O Abu Rafi', catch up with him and do not leave him from behind; let him halt and not turn until I come to him. He came to him and enjoined things upon him, saying: O Ali, that Allah guide a man through your hands is better for you than all upon which the sun has risen."
"996","Abu Asma, freedman of the family of Ja'far, from Abu Rafi'. 995 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami, from Abu Asma, freedman of the family of Ja'far, from Abu Rafi', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): There shall be between you and A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) an affair. He said: I, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: I among your companions? He said: Yes. He said: Then am I the most wretched of them? He said: No, but when that happens, return her to her place of safety."
"997","90 - Ibrahim ibn Khallad ibn Suwayd al-Khazraji. 996 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd narrated, my uncle narrated, my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Ibrahim ibn Khallad ibn Suwayd al-Khazraji, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, be loud-voiced and free-flowing (in talbiyah and sacrifice)."
"998","Ibrahim Abu Ata al-Ta'ifi. 997 - Ahmad ibn Mabihram al-Idhaji narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz narrated, Yahya ibn Ata ibn Ibrahim, a man of Ta'if, narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina addressing the people, saying to them: Pair up the sandals."
"999","92 - From Arta'ah ibn al-Mundhir al-Sakuni, and it is said: Laqit ibn Arta'ah. 998 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated, Nasr ibn Alqamah narrated, from Ibn A'idh, from his brother Arta'ah ibn al-Mundhir al-Sakuni, that a visitor came to him and said: We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits indecency; shall I report his affair to the ruler? He said: I killed ninety-nine polytheists before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it would not please me to have killed the like of them and to have uncovered the veil of a Muslim."
"1000","93 - al-Asqa' al-Bakri. 999 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, Umar ibn Ata informed me, that the freedman of Ibn al-Asqa', a truthful man, informed him, from al-Asqa' al-Bakri, that he heard him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them in the Suffah of the Emigrants; a man asked him: Which verse in the Qur'an is greatest? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer; neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes Him."
"1001","94 - Aslam ibn Bajrah al-Ansari, then al-Khazraji. 1000 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Ayyash informed me, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Aslam ibn Bajrah al-Ansari, he was informed by his father, from Aslam ibn Bajrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he placed him over the captives of Qurayzah; he would look at a boy's private part, and if he saw him grown with hair he struck his neck, and took whoever had not grown hair and placed him among the spoils of the Muslims."
"1002","95 - Asad ibn Kurz al-Bajali, then al-Qushayri. 1001 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Arta'ah ibn al-Mundhir, from al-Muhasir ibn Habib al-Zubaydi, from Asad ibn Kurz, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Asad ibn Kurz, you shall not enter Paradise by deeds, but by Allah's mercy. I said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelop me - or enfold me - from Him with mercy."
"1003","1002 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated, (H) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, (H) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Suran narrated, they said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, Isma'il ibn Awsat narrated, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from his grandfather Asad ibn Kurz, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Illness removes sins as the leaves of a tree fall."
"1004","96 - Azhar Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri. 1003 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated, he said: I found in my maternal uncle's book, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, he was informed, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar al-Zuhri informed him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drinker while at Khaybar; he threw dust in his face, then ordered his companions and they beat him with their sandals and whatever was in their hands, until he said to them: Lift him. So they lifted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away with that as his practice. Then Abu Bakr lashed forty for wine; then Umar (may Allah Almighty be pleased with him) lashed forty at the beginning of his rule, then lashed eighty at the end of his caliphate; then Uthman (may Allah Almighty be pleased with him) lashed the hadd forty; then Mu'awiyah (may Allah Almighty be pleased with him) eighty."
"1005","1004 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Bakr ibn Sawwadah, from Muslim ibn Makhshi, from Ibn al-Firasi, that his father al-Firasi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I beg? He said: No; and if you must beg, then beg the righteous."
"1006","Chapter of Ba. 97 - Bilal ibn Rabah, caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he attended Badr, kunya Abu Abd Allah. 1005 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr: the freedman of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1007","1006 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr: Bilal, freedman of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1008","1007 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Bilal, freedman of Abu Bakr - and it is said he is the age-mate of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) - died at Damascus in the plague, buried at the Small Gate, kunya Abu Abd Allah, in the year seventeen or eighteen; he is of the home-born of al-Sarah; and it is said: Bilal, kunya Abu Amr."
"1009","1008 - And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) freed seven of those tortured for Allah, among them Bilal and Amir ibn Fuhayrah."
"1010","1009 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated, Muhammad ibn Muhajir al-Ansari narrated, Umayr ibn Hani narrated, from Hind, wife of Bilal, she said: When Bilal took his bed he would say: O Allah, overlook my evils and excuse me for my infirmities."
"1011","1010 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Bilal said to Abu Bakr when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away (may Allah be pleased with them both): If you bought me for yourself, keep me; and if you freed me for Allah, let me work for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"1012","1011 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Bilal came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was in Syria with the commanders of the armies seated around him. He said: O Umar - here I am, Umar. Bilal said: You are between Allah and these people, and there is no one between you and Allah; look to your right, your left, before you and behind you - these around you eat nothing but birds' meat. He said: You spoke truly; by Allah, I shall not rise from this sitting of mine until you undertake for each Muslim man his food and his share of oil and vinegar. They said: This is upon you, O Commander of the Faithful, for Allah has widened provision for us and multiplied good."
"1013","1012 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard a footfall before me when I entered Paradise. I said: Who is this? They said: Bilal. He informed him and said: By what do you precede me to Paradise? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I never innovated impurity except I performed ablution, and never performed ablution except I prayed two rak'ahs following the ablution."
"1014","1013 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, Umar and Ammar, sons of Hafs, from their fathers, from their grandfathers, they said: Bilal came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best deed of the believer is jihad in the path of Allah; and I want to bind myself in the path of Allah until I die. Abu Bakr said: I adjure you by Allah, O Bilal, and by my sanctity and right - my age has grown great, my strength weakened, my term drawn near. Bilal stayed with him. When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, Umar came; he said to him what Abu Bakr had said, but Bilal refused him. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: To whom then, O Bilal? He said: To Sa'd, for he called the adhan at Quba in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Umar assigned the adhan to Sa'd and Uqbah."
"1015","1014 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, he said: I heard Isma'il, he mentioned it from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Mudrik ibn Awf, he said: I passed by Bilal while he was sitting at dawn prayer. I said: What detains you, O Abu Abd Allah? He said: I await the rising of the sun."
"1016","Muhammad ibn Ali Fustuqah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: Umar said: Abu Bakr is our master, and he freed our master, meaning Bilal."
"1017","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, pray the dawn prayer at daybreak, for that is better for you."
"1018","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), from Bilal, who said: I had in my keeping some dates belonging to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they deteriorated, so I took them out to the market and sold two sas for one sa. When I brought some of it near to him, he said: What is this, O Bilal? So I informed him. He said: Wait, undo the sale, then sell dates for gold or silver or wheat, then buy dates with it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dates for dates, like for like; wheat for wheat, like for like; gold for gold, weight for weight; silver for silver, weight for weight; but when the two kinds differ there is no harm, one for ten."
"1019","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hamzah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Bilal, who said: I had some inferior dates, so I bought with them in the market dates better than them for half their measure, and I presented them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I have not seen today dates better than these; where did you get these from, O Bilal? He said: So I told him what I had done. He said: Go and return it to its owner and take your dates, then sell them for wheat or barley, then buy these dates with it, then bring them to me. He said: So I did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dates for dates, like for like; wheat for wheat, like for like; barley for barley, like for like; salt for salt, like for like; gold for gold, like for like, weight for weight; silver for silver, like for like, weight for weight; whatever is extra is usury."
"1020","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from al-Hakam, from Shurayh ibn Hani, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Bilal claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the muqs and the khimar."
"1021","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, both saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi informed us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal while he had a heap of dates with him, and he said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I stored it for you and your guests. He said: Do you not fear that a vapor from Hell will come to it? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Lord of the Throne."
"1022","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Imran ibn Aban narrated to us, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Abu al-Mubarak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Bilal, die poor and do not die rich. I said: And how is that? He said: Whatever you are given, do not store it away, and whatever you are asked for, do not withhold. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, how can I manage that? He said: That is it, or the Fire."
"1023","And with his chain, from Abu Said, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I had some dates with me, and he said: What is this? So I said: We stored it for our winter. He said: Do you not fear that you will see its vapor in Hell?"
"1024","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs."
"1025","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Muhammad al-Sirini narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal and found with him heaps of dates, and he said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: Dates I am storing. He said: Woe to you, O Bilal, do you not fear that it will have a vapor in the Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Lord of the Throne."
"1026","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Bilal when he was ill, and he brought out for him a heap of dates. He said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: I stored it for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not fear that a vapor in the fire of Hell will be made for you? Spend, Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Lord of the Throne."
"1027","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal, and he mentioned similar to it."
"1028","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque of Quba, and the Ansar came greeting him. So I said to Bilal: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) respond to them? He said: Like this, gesturing with his hand."
"1029","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Abu Duhqabah narrated to us, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar, and Ibn Umar mentioned that Bilal narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited by a guest, so he ordered him to bring him food, so he brought him dates, and those dates pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Where did you get these dates from? He said: I exchanged one sa for two sas. He said: Return our dates to us. So he returned them."
"1030","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha informed me, from his father, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking between Usamah and Bilal until they both entered the Kabah, and in it was a crossbeam of wood. When Bilal came out I asked him: What did he do? He said: He left two thirds of the beam to his right and prayed in the remaining third. I said: How many did he pray? He said: I did not ask Bilal about that."
"1031","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he asked Bilal about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inside the House, and he informed him that he prayed two rakahs in the middle of the House, placing the pillar to his right, advancing a little, and placing the Maqam behind his back."
"1032","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, and Bilal stood at the door. Ibn Umar said: So I asked Bilal: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Yes, two rakahs in the middle of the House."
"1033","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Ibn Umar, that he reported from Bilal that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs in it."
"1034","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Kabah."
"1035","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, with another chain, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House."
"1036","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah and others narrating this hadith, some of them adding to others. He said: Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came on the day of the Conquest upon a camel belonging to Usamah ibn Zayd, with Usamah riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him were Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Usamah ibn Zayd, Uthman ibn Talhah and Bilal entered, and they stayed in the House a long time and closed the door upon themselves. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, and they rushed to the door, and Abdullah ibn Umar and another man with him outran them. Abdullah ibn Umar asked Bilal: Where did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? So he showed him where he had prayed, and he did not ask him how many he had prayed."
"1037","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim informed me, both saying: Uthman ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House facing its front, then stood and supplicated for a while, then left."
"1038","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Waki narrated to us, from al-Saib ibn Umar, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I asked Bilal: Where did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray when he entered the Kabah? He said: Between the two pillars."
"1039","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I said to Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray, meaning inside the House? He said: Between the two front pillars, praying two rakahs."
"1040","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived and stayed in the courtyard of the Kabah, then sent for Uthman ibn Talhah, who came with the key. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Bilal, Usamah ibn Zayd and Uthman ibn Talhah entered. When they came out, the people rushed to them, so I said to Bilal: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray inside the House? He said: Yes, between the two pillars facing his front."
"1041","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I said to Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two pillars."
"1042","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, he and Usamah ibn Zayd, Uthman ibn Talhah al-Hajabi and Bilal, and he closed it upon them, and stayed in it. Abdullah ibn Umar said: So I asked Bilal when he came out: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do? He said: He placed a pillar to his left, two pillars to his right, and three pillars behind him, and the House at that time was upon six pillars, then he prayed."
"1043","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came on the day of the Conquest upon a she-camel belonging to Usamah ibn Zayd, with Usamah riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him were Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah. When he came to the House he sent Uthman ibn Talhah, who brought him the key of the House and opened it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Usamah, Uthman ibn Talhah and Bilal entered, and they stayed in the House a long time, closing the House upon themselves. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, and the people rushed to the House, and Abdullah ibn Umar and another man with him outran them. Abdullah ibn Umar asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? So Bilal showed him where he had prayed, but he did not ask how many he had prayed."
"1044","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah with Bilal, Usamah and Uthman with him, and he had closed the door upon them. I came and sat on the ground, and they stayed in it a while. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, I climbed the stairs and entered the House, and I said: Where did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? They said: Here, and I forgot to ask how many he had prayed."
"1045","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed when he entered the House. He said: Between these two pillars that are nearest the door."
"1046","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Farqad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, with Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah, and stayed in the House a long time, then came out. Abdullah ibn Umar entered right after him, before all the people, and asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars, and I forgot to ask him how many he had prayed."
"1047","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya, scribe of al-Umari, narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Tawil, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, he and Usamah ibn Zayd, Uthman ibn Talhah and Bilal, and stayed in the House a long time, then came out. Abdullah entered right after him, before all the people, and asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two pillars."
"1048","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from al-Awzai, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, Nafi, the freedman of Ibn Umar, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah on the day of the Conquest with Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah ibn Shaybah, and they closed it upon themselves from inside. When they came out I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He informed me that he prayed facing his front when he entered, placing the two pillars to his right. He said: Then I blamed myself for not having asked him how many he had prayed."
"1049","Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1050","Abu Salih al-Qasim ibn al-Layth al-Rasibi narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Usamah riding behind him upon al-Adba, and with him were Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah, until he made his camel kneel at the House. He said to Uthman: Bring us the key. So he brought him the key, and he opened the door for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Usamah, Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah entered, then they closed the House upon themselves, and stayed in it a long time, then came out. The people rushed to enter, and I outran them. I found Bilal standing behind the people, so I said: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: He prayed between the two front pillars, placing the people behind his back, and facing with his face the direction you are facing."
"1051","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, with another chain, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Hushaym narrated to us, al-Hajjaj and Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter the House with a group: Usamah ibn Zayd, al-Fadl ibn Abbas, Uthman ibn Talhah and Bilal, and he closed the door. I stood at the door. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, the first one to meet me was Bilal. So I said: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two pillars."
"1052","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, with another chain, and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, both saying: Juwayriyah ibn Asma narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah with Usamah ibn Zayd, Uthman ibn Talhah and Bilal, and stayed there a long time. I was the first of the people to enter after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said to Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Two rakahs between the two front pillars."
"1053","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Two rakahs between the two pillars."
"1054","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah with Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal, and with him the doorkeeper of the Kabah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, I was the first to enter. I found Bilal at the door, and asked him: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars."
"1055","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House, and with him entered al-Fadl ibn Abbas, Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah, and he stayed a long time, then came out. I rushed ahead of the people and was among the first to enter. I met Bilal and said: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars. Ibn Umar said: And I forgot to ask him how many he had prayed."
"1056","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House, he and Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah, and they closed it upon themselves. When they opened, I was among the first to enter. I met Bilal and said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in it? He said: Yes, he prayed between the two Yemeni pillars."
"1057","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, who said: I was with my father, and we met Abdullah ibn Umar. My father asked him while I was listening: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray when he entered the House? Ibn Umar said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered between Usamah and Bilal. When they both came out, I asked them both: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? They said: On its front side."
"1058","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Shair narrated to me, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Yahya ibn Jada, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, so I set out quickly and met Bilal. I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray inside the House? He said: Yes, he prayed two rakahs between the two pillars, placing the right pillar to his right."
"1059","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, who said: I heard Ikrimah ibn Khalid and Jubayr ibn Shaybah ibn Uthman ibn Abd al-Dar, that Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray when he entered the House? Ibn Umar said: I did not find him while he was praying; I came when he had finished. So I asked Bilal, and he informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed between two pillars."
"1060","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Umar, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a servant named Rabah."
"1061","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, with another chain, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani narrated to us, with another chain, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, all saying: Abu Muawiyah informed us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the muqs and the khimar."
"1062","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, with another chain, and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, all of them from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1063","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from Bilal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1064","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and the two socks."
"1065","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Usamah ibn Zayd and Abdullah ibn Rawahah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house of Haml, he and Bilal, then Bilal came out to them and informed them both that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had performed ablution and wiped over the two khuffs."
"1066","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Bilal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the two khuffs."
"1067","Abu Husayn al-Qadi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir, Bilal the muezzin narrated to me, who said: I called the adhan on a cold night and no one came, then I called out and no one came, three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with them? So I said: The cold prevented them. He said: O Allah, lift the cold from them. Bilal said: I bear witness that I saw them fanning themselves in the morning because of the heat."
"1068","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Yaman narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, pray the dawn prayer at daybreak, for that is better for you."
"1069","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, Makhul informed me, that Nuaym ibn Hammar informed him, that Bilal informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wipe over the two khuffs and over the khimar."
"1070","Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Makhul, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1071","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakam narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: Bilal said: We were not forbidden from praying at any time except when the sun is rising, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, or upon the two horns of Satan."
"1072","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Ammar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, and Umar and Ammar, the two sons of Hafs, from their fathers, from their grandfathers, from Bilal, that he used to call the adhan for the dawn prayer, saying: Come to the best of deeds. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to put in its place: Prayer is better than sleep, and to leave out: Come to the best of deeds."
"1073","And with his chain, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you call the adhan, put your finger in your ears, for that raises your voice more."
"1074","And from Bilal, that he used to call the adhan for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to call the adhan: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; then he would turn away from the right of the qiblah, saying: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; then he would turn and face behind the qiblah, saying: Come to prayer, come to prayer; then he would turn to his left, saying: Come to success, come to success; then he would face the qiblah, saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah. And he used to call the iqamah for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), making the iqamah single, saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to success; the prayer has begun; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah."
"1075","Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: The last adhan of Bilal was: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"1076","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yala ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sad, relating from his father Sad, the muezzin of Umar, from Bilal, that he used to call the adhan for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday when the shade was the length of a sandal-strap, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the minbar."
"1077","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Ammar the muezzin narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, and Ammar and Umar, the two sons of Hafs ibn Umar, from their fathers, from Bilal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best deed of the believer is jihad in the path of Allah."
"1078","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, with another chain, and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Amr ibn Bishr narrated to us, with another chain, and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awsabi al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, all from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has placed the truth upon the tongue and heart of Umar."
"1079","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him of the prayer once, and it was said: He is sleeping. So he called out: Prayer is better than sleep, and it was approved in the Fajr prayer."
"1080","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Bilal, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and they slept until the sun rose. So he ordered Bilal, who called the adhan, then they prayed the two rakahs of Fajr, then they prayed the morning prayer."
"1081","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, with another chain, and Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, Abu Imran Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi narrated to them, that Qabisah ibn Dhuayb al-Khuzai narrated to him, from Bilal, that he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), people trade and pursue their livelihoods, and we are unable to do that. He said: Are you not pleased that the muezzins will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection?"
"1082","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Hafs ibn Umar, from Bilal, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him of the dawn prayer and found him sleeping. He said: Prayer is better than sleep, twice. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How good this is, O Bilal; put it in your adhan."
"1083","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Maqil, from Bilal, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him of the prayer while he intended to fast. He drank, then handed to me and I drank, then he went out to the prayer and led us in prayer."
"1084","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Bahr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Maqil, from Bilal, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him of the prayer while he intended to fast. He called for a vessel and drank, then handed to me and I drank, then he went out to the prayer."
"1085","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud Sandilah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Abu Yusuf, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Bilal, raising it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He raised his gaze to the sky and said: Glory be to Allah who sends poverty upon them like the sending of rain."
"1086","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated to me, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Bilal, that he saw a man praying badly, not completing its bowing nor its prostration, and said: If you died now you would die upon other than the religion of Isa (peace be upon him)."
"1087","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and over the khimar."
"1088","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla and Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over the muqs and the khimar."
"1089","Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, with another chain, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, with another chain, and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated to us, all saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his two khuffs and the turban."
"1090","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman, from Bilal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two khuffs and over the khimar."
"1091","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1092","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Maymun Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Bilal, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two khuffs."
"1093","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to say the tathwib in Fajr, and forbade me from saying the tathwib in Isha."
"1094","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, from Abu Israil, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to say the tathwib in Fajr, and forbade me from saying the tathwib in Isha."
"1095","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Naqid narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ziyad al-Bakkai narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, who said: Bilal narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, so when you see that, hasten to prayer."
"1096","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Musaddad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1097","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Musaddad narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Hakam and Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Shurayh ibn Hani, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1098","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Bilal, who said: I had dates belonging to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I found better than them at one sa for two sas. So I bought them and brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What is this? So I said: I took one sa for two sas. He said: Return our dates to us."
"1099","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed us dates, O Bilal. So I scooped handfuls for him. He said: Give us more, O Bilal. So I gave him three more, and I said: Nothing remains except something I stored for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Lord of the Throne."
"1100","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayh, Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar narrated to me, Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah informed me, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf asking Bilal: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the two khuffs? He said: He relieved himself, then called for water for purification in a water-skin, washed his face and hands, then wiped over his two khuffs and over his khimar because of the turban."
"1101","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, with another chain, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, a shaykh from Banu Taym named Abu Abdullah narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was with Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf when Bilal passed, and they asked him about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He would relieve himself, then come and perform ablution, wiping over the khimar and the muqs."
"1102","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Abdullah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1103","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Naji narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from al-Sunabihi, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-fourth."
"1104","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah and Suhayl ibn Abi Jandal, that they both asked Bilal about wiping, and he said: Wipe over the khumurs and the muq, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1105","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah and Suhayl ibn Abi Jandal, that they both asked Bilal about wiping, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wipe over the khumurs and the muq."
"1106","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah and from Abu Jandal al-Qurashi, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the muqs and the khimar."
"1107","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Ubayd al-Kalai, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah and Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl, who said: We asked Bilal about wiping over the two khuffs, and Bilal said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wipe over the two khuffs and the muq."
"1108","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1109","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah, from Muawiyah al-Kinani, who said: He and a man from Quraysh were performing ablution from the water vessel of the mosque, and they disputed about wiping over the two khuffs. Bilal said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the muqs and the khimar."
"1110","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah and Abu Jandal, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1111","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, that Bilal, the freedman of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he came from relieving himself on the day of the Tabuk expedition, called for water for ablution, and wiped over the two khuffs."
"1112","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, with another chain, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Umar ibn Amir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Jandal, from Bilal, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the muqs and the khimar."
"1113","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Idris, from Bilal, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the turban and the muqs."
"1114","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: Bilal wiped over his muqs. It was said to him: What is this? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two khuffs and the khimar. Mamar did not mention Abu Idris in his hadith, and likewise Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated it from Abu Qilabah."
"1115","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Qilabah, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1116","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Abu Raja, from his uncle Abu Idris, that he was sitting in Damascus on a cold day performing ablution, and Bilal, the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), passed by him. He said: O Bilal, how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution? He said: He would wipe over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1117","Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Muqri al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Abu Raja, the freedman of Abu Qilabah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Idris, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1118","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Idris, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1119","Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani and Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, both saying: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Abu Qilabah al-Jarmi, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"1120","Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Abdullah al-Hawzani narrated to me, who said: I met Bilal, the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: O Bilal, tell me how the spending of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. He said: He had nothing; I was the one who managed that for him since Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent him, until he died. When a Muslim person came to him and he saw him naked, he would order me regarding him, so I would go and borrow, buy a cloak, clothe him and feed him, until a man from the polytheists met me and said: O Bilal, I have means, so do not borrow from anyone except me. So I did. One day I performed ablution, then stood to call the adhan for prayer, and the polytheist came with a group of merchants. When he saw me he said: O Habashi! I said: At your service. He frowned at me and said to me a grave word. He said: Do you know how much is between you and the month? I said: Near. He said: Between you and it are only four days, and I will seize you for what you owe me, for I did not give you what I gave out of your honor nor the honor of your companion to me, but I gave you only to take you as my slave, returning you to herd sheep as you were before that. Something seized my soul like what seizes the souls of people. I went, then called the adhan for prayer until I prayed Isha. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his family, so I asked permission to see him and he permitted me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheist from whom I had borrowed said to me such and such, and you have nothing to pay on my behalf, nor do I, and he will disgrace me. So permit me to flee to some of these tribes who have embraced Islam until Allah provides His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with what will pay on my behalf. I went out until I came to my house, placed my sword, bag, shield and sandals at my head, faced the horizon with my face, and whenever I slept an hour I woke; when I saw night still upon me I slept, until the first column of dawn split. I wanted to leave, when a man came hurrying, calling: O Bilal, answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I went until I came to him, and there were four kneeling camels with their loads upon them. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked permission. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Rejoice, for Allah has brought you your payment. I praised Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. He said: Did you not pass by the four kneeling camels? I said: Yes. He said: Their necks are yours, and what is upon them of clothing and food, gifted to me by the chief of Fadak. Take them, then pay your debt. So I did: I unloaded their loads from them, then hobbled them, then stood to call the Fajr prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, I went out to al-Baqi, put my fingers in my ears, called out: Whoever has a debt upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him come. I kept selling and paying until no debt remained upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on earth, until two uqiyyahs, or an uqiyyah and a half, remained in my hand. Then I went to the mosque when most of the day had gone, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque alone. I greeted him. He said to me: What happened to what was with you? I said: Allah has paid everything that was upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); nothing remains. He said: Did anything remain? I said: Yes. He said: See that you relieve me of it, for I shall not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of it. No one came to us until evening. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha he called me and said to me: What happened to what was with you? I said: It is with me; no one came to us. He spent the night in the mosque until morning, and remained the second day until at the end of the day two riders came. I took them, fed them and clothed them. When he prayed Isha he called me and said: What happened to what was with you? I said: Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah. He magnified Allah and praised Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, out of fear that death would overtake him while that was with him. Then I followed him until he came to his wives, greeting woman by woman until he came to his lodging. That is what you asked me about."
"1121","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Sallam, Ibn Sallam narrated to me, from Ghaylan al-Thaqafi, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1122","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Shaddad, the freedman of Iyad, from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call the adhan until you see the dawn like this, and he gestured with his hand, then opened it."
"1123","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ayyub ibn al-Ala informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"1124","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydillah al-Shami, from Abu Mulaykah al-Dhimari, from Nimran al-Yahsabi, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, call out among the people: whoever says There is no god but Allah a year before his death will enter Paradise, or a month, or a week, or a day, or an hour. He said: Then they will rely on it. He said: Even if they rely on it."
"1125","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, that Bilal said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not precede me with Amin."
"1126","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Main narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Bilal, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not precede me with Amin."
"1127","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, Bishr ibn Muhammad al-Umawi informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good deed is charity."
"1128","Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, who said: Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani died in the year sixty, at the age of eighty."
"1129","Muhammad ibn Ali Fustuqah narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdillah al-Hammal narrated to us, who said: Bilal ibn al-Harith is known as Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"1130","Idris ibn Jafar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached, and Allah writes for him His pleasure because of it until the Day of Resurrection. And a man speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not seeing that it will reach what it reached, and Allah writes for him His wrath because of it until the day he meets Him."
"1131","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: One of you speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes for him His pleasure until the Day of Resurrection. And one of you speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes upon him His wrath because of it until the Day of Resurrection."
"1132","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin al-Basri narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not seeing that it reached what it reached, and Allah writes for him His pleasure because of it until the Day of Resurrection. And a man speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not seeing that it reaches what it reaches, and Allah writes upon him His wrath because of it until the day he meets Him."
"1133","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: One of you speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes for him His pleasure because of it until the day he meets Him. And one of you speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes upon him His wrath until the day he meets Him."
"1134","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, my grandfather Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not seeing that it will reach what it reached, and his wrath is written for him until the Day of Resurrection. And a man speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not seeing that it will reach what it reached, and His pleasure is written for him until the day he meets Him."
"1135","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1136","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from his father Amr ibn Alqamah, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes for him His pleasure because of it until the day he meets Him. And a man speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes upon him His wrath because of it until the day he meets Him."
"1137","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, with another chain, and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, with another chain, and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hakam narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from his father, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks a word pleasing to Allah, never thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes for him His pleasure until the day he meets Him. And a man speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, never thinking it will reach what it reached; Allah writes for him His wrath because of it until the day he meets Him. Abu al-Qasim said: Malik and Muhammad ibn Ajlan dropped Alqamah ibn Waqqas, the grandfather of Muhammad ibn Amr, from the chain, while Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it differing from the people in it."
"1138","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks a word of the wrath of Allah, not knowing how far it reached, and Allah writes for him His wrath because of it until the day he meets Him. And a man speaks a word pleasing to Allah, not knowing how far it reached, and Allah writes for him His pleasure because of it until the day he meets Him."
"1139","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Shahriyar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Amir ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Alqamah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man speaks a word of good, not knowing its reach; Allah writes for him His pleasure because of it until the day he meets Him. And a man speaks a word of evil, not knowing its reach; Allah writes upon him His wrath because of it until the day he meets Him."
"1140","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"1141","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is the cancellation of Hajj for us specifically, or for people generally? He said: Rather, for us specifically."
"1142","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Rabiah, from al-Harith ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by the oath along with the witness."
"1143","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdillah narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zabalah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Rabiah, from al-Harith ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him all of al-Aqiq as a land grant."
"1144","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Humayd ibn Salih narrated to me, from Umarah and Bilal, the two sons of Yahya ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith, from their father, from their grandfather Bilal ibn al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him this land grant and wrote for him: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), gave Bilal ibn al-Harith: he gave him the mines of al-Qabiliyyah, its lowlands and its highlands, Ghashiyyah and Dhat al-Nusub, and wherever cultivation is suitable of Quds, if he is truthful. And Muawiyah wrote it."
"1145","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both saying: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdillah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, he would go far."
"1146","Khalid ibn al-Nadr al-Qurashi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys. He went out to relieve himself, and when he went out to relieve himself he would go far. I brought him a water-skin of water. He went on, and I heard near him a dispute of men and a clamor the like of which I had never heard. He came and said: Bilal. I said: Bilal. He said: Do you have water with you? I said: Yes. He said: You did right. He took it from me and performed ablution. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard near you a dispute of men and a clamor whose tongues I never heard sharper. He said: The Muslim jinn and the polytheist jinn disputed before me; they asked me to settle them, so I settled the Muslims in al-Jalas and the polytheists in al-Ghawr. Abdullah ibn Kathir said: I said to Kathir: What are al-Jalas and al-Ghawr? He said: Al-Jalas are the towns and mountains, and al-Ghawr is what is between the mountains and the seas. Kathir said: We never saw anyone afflicted in al-Jalas except that he was safe, and no one was afflicted in al-Ghawr except that he hardly was safe."
"1147","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Nasr al-Tusi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Makhrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Kathir ibn Jafar narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Ramadan in Madinah is better than a thousand Ramadans in other lands, and a Friday in Madinah is better than a thousand Fridays in other lands."
"1148","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdillah Abu Musa narrated to us, who said: Buraydah ibn al-Husayb al-Aslami died in Khurasan during the caliphate of Yazid ibn Muawiyah, in the year sixty-two. Abu Musa said: And Buraydah ibn Husayb is known as Abu Abdullah."
"1149","Al-Hasan ibn Sahl ibn Hurayth al-Misri narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Samurah ibn Hujr narrated to us, Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Buraydah, there will be expeditions, so join the expedition of Khurasan, then join the city of Marw, for no evil will befall its people, because Dhu al-Qarnayn built it."
"1150","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ata al-Khurasani, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter. I forbade you from earthenware jars, so drink in every vessel but avoid every intoxicant. I forbade you from eating the meat of sacrifices after three days, so eat, take provision, and store."
"1151","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ruwasi narrated to us, Abd al-Karim ibn Salit narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: A group of the Ansar said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): You have Fatimah. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. He said: What does the son of Abu Talib need? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I mentioned Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Welcome and congratulations. He did not add to that. Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) went out to those men of the Ansar waiting for him. They said: And what was that? He said: I do not know, except that he said to me: Welcome and congratulations. They said: One of the two from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) suffices you: he gave you family and welcome. Later, after he married her to him, he said: O Ali, the bridegroom must have a wedding feast. Sad said: I have a ram. A group of the Ansar collected for him sas of corn. On the night of consummation he said: Do not do anything until you meet me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, performed ablution from it, then poured it upon Ali and said: O Allah, bless them both, and bless them both in their union."
"1152","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Judges are three: two judges in the Fire, and one judge in Paradise. A judge who judged unjustly while knowing, that one is in the Fire. A judge who judged while not knowing, destroying the rights of people, that one is in the Fire. And a judge who judged with truth, that one is in Paradise."
"1153","Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, from Rumayh ibn Hilal al-Tai, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, who said: We prayed Zuhr behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he finished his prayer he turned to us angry, calling out with a voice that made the maidens in the chambers hear. He said: O company of those who embraced Islam while faith has not entered their hearts, do not revile the Muslims, nor seek their faults, for whoever seeks the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah will tear his cover and expose his fault, even if he is inside the cover of his house."
"1154","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Judges are three: two judges in the Fire, and one judge in Paradise. A judge who judged unjustly while knowing is in the Fire. A judge who judged unjustly while not knowing is in the Fire. And a judge who judged with truth while knowing is in Paradise. Abu al-Qasim said: Abdullah ibn Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, differed from the people regarding this man, saying: Abbad, while al-Mutayyan, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, al-Tirmidhi and others narrated from him, saying: Ubadah ibn Ziyad."
"1155","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the market he would say: O Allah, I ask You for the good of this market and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from striking in it a wicked oath or a losing bargain."
"1156","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A stone will weigh seven pregnant she-camels, cast into Hell, falling seventy autumns without reaching its bottom."
"1157","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Abdillah, the custodian of charity, narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys, he came upon a man rolling in the scorching heat, back to belly, saying: O soul, sleep by night and falsehood by day, and you hope to enter Paradise? When he finished with himself he came to us and said: Take your brother. We said: Supplicate to Allah for us, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: O Allah, unite their affair upon guidance. We said: Add more. He said: O Allah, make piety their provision. We said: Add more. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Add more. He said: O Allah, grant them success. He said: O Allah, make Paradise their return."
"1158","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and he gestured to us with his hand to sit."
"1159","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hayyan ibn Ubaydillah Abu Zuhayr al-Adawi narrated to us, Abu Mijlaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, Hayyan said: And Ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, that the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black, and his flag was white."
"1160","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr al-Rumi narrated to us, Abu Muslim, the guide of al-Amash, narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, raising it, who said: Al-Samad is the One who has no hollow."
"1161","1163 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a dog be named Kalb, or Kulayb."
"1162","1164 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Amr ibn Rafi' Abu Hujr al-Qazwini narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Dashtaki narrated to us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The superiority of the wives of the mujahidin over those who stay behind in sanctity is like that of their mothers, and there is no one among those who stay behind who takes the place of one of the mujahidin among his family and betrays him regarding them, except that he will be made to stand before him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: This one betrayed you regarding your family, so take from his deeds whatever you wish."
"1163","100 - Bara ibn Azib al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 1165 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I and Ibn Umar were deemed too young on the day of Badr."
"1164","1166 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my uncle Abu Bakr narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I and Ibn Umar were presented on the day of Badr before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he deemed us too young, and we were present at Uhud."
"1165","1167 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I and Ibn Umar were deemed too young on the day of Badr."
"1166","1168 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I and Ibn Umar were deemed too young on the day of Badr and we did not witness it."
"1167","1169 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abu Janab al-Kalbi narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Bara narrated to me, from his father, who said: We were sitting, waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Adha, then he came and greeted the people and said: The first rite of this day of yours is the prayer. Then he went forward and prayed two rak'as with the people, then greeted, then faced the people, then he was given a bow or a staff and leaned on it, then praised Allah Almighty, extolled Him, commanded them and forbade them."
"1168","1170 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Isra'il al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when morning and evening came: We have entered morning and sovereignty belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah, there is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him. O Allah, we ask You for the good of this day and the good of what is after it, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this day and the evil of what is after it. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and the evil of old age, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire."
"1169","1171 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Darmak ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of loneliness, so he said: Say: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit, You have covered the heavens and the earth with might and omnipotence. So the man said it, and Allah Almighty removed the loneliness from him."
"1170","1172 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: Al-Bara ibn Azib said to me: Shall I not teach you a supplication taught to me by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: When you see people competing over gold and silver, supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, I ask You for firmness in the matter, and I ask You for strong resolve in guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing, and patience upon Your trial, and excellence in Your worship, and contentment with Your decree, and I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You of the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know."
"1171","1173 - Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: What is your name? He said: Nu'm. He said: Rather, you are Abdullah."
"1172","1174 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn al-Husayn al-Saluli narrated to us, al-Sabiyy ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the traveller, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night, regarding wiping over the khuffs."
"1173","1175 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Hurayth, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq and al-Bara, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it, and if it is obscured for you then complete thirty. And he said with his hand: The month is like this and like this, meaning twenty-nine."
"1174","1176 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Dinar al-Harashi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Qays al-Kindi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Juhayfa, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That he forbade the price of a dog, and the dowry of a prostitute, and the earning of a cupper, and the fee of a soothsayer, and the stud fee of a stallion. And al-Bara had a he-goat which whoever sought would use for mating, he would not refuse anyone, nor would he take a fee for the stallion."
"1175","1177 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we came upon a well with little water - Sulayman said: al-Dhimma means little water - he said: So six of us went down, I being the sixth of them, or seven, I being the seventh of them, as drawers of water - Sulayman said: al-Maha are those who draw water - he said: So we let down a bucket, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the edge of the well, and we placed in it half of it, or he said: about two-thirds of it or similar, then it was lifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bara said: So I scraped my vessel, seeking whether I could find something to put in my throat, but I found nothing. He said: So it was lifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he dipped his hand in it and said whatever Allah willed him to say. Then the bucket was returned to it with the water in it. He said: I saw each one of us taken out with his garment for fear of drowning, then it flowed - or he said: it welled up - and the wording is that of the hadith of al-Muqri."
"1176","101 - Bara ibn Malik, brother of Anas ibn Malik. 1178 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Al-Bara ibn Malik lay on his back, then sang, so Anas said to him: O my brother. So he sat upright and said: O Anas, do you think I will die on my bed, when I have killed one hundred of the polytheists in single combat, besides those in whose killing I shared."
"1177","1179 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, in the year two hundred and ninety, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, who said: Anas visited al-Bara ibn Malik while he was reciting poetry, so he said: O my brother, Allah has taught you what is better for you than it. He said: Yes. So al-Bara said to him: Do you fear I will die on my bed? By Allah, that will not be Allah afflicting me, for I have killed one hundred of the polytheists, not alone in killing them, and among them are those in whose killing I shared."
"1178","1180 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Al-Bara ibn Malik, brother of Anas ibn Malik, fought in single combat Marzuban al-Zara and killed him, then took his spoils, and his spoils reached thirty thousand. That reached Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he said to Abu Talha: We used not to take a fifth from spoils taken in single combat, but the spoils of al-Bara have reached much wealth, so I see no option but to take a fifth of it."
"1179","1181 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Al-Bara ibn Malik met on the day of Musaylima a man called Himar al-Yamama. He said: A tall man in whose hand was a white sword. He said: And al-Bara was a short man, so al-Bara struck his legs with the sword, as if he missed him, and he fell on his back. He said: So I took his sword and sheathed my sword, and I struck only one blow until it broke, so I threw it away and took my sword."
"1180","1182 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir, brother of Isma'il ibn Ja'far, narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salama al-Majishun, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha, who said: While Anas ibn Malik and his brother al-Bara ibn Malik were at one of the fortresses of the enemy, and the enemy were casting hooks on heated chains, which would catch a man and they would lift him to them, one of those hooks caught Anas ibn Malik and they lifted him until he was raised from the ground. So his brother al-Bara ibn Malik was approached and told: Catch up with your brother, while he was fighting among the people. So he came running until he leapt onto the wall, then grasped the chain with his hand while it was turning, and kept pulling them with his hands smoking until he cut the rope. Then he looked at his hands, and the bones were visible, the flesh on them gone. And Allah Almighty saved Anas ibn Malik thereby."
"1181","102 - Bara ibn Ma'rur al-Ansari, then al-Sulami. 1183 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of the companions of al-Aqaba who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu Salama ibn Yazid ibn Jusham: al-Bara ibn Ma'rur ibn Sakhr ibn Khansa, and he was a naqib, and he was the first who bequeathed a third of his wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted it."
"1182","1184 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, regarding those who witnessed al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu Salama: al-Bara ibn Ma'rur, and he was the first who bequeathed a third of his wealth and faced the Ka'ba while in his land, and he was a naqib."
"1183","1185 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'bad, or Abu Muhammad ibn Ma'bad, narrated to us, from Abu Qatada, that al-Bara ibn Ma'rur bequeathed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a third of his wealth, to place it wherever he wished, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it to his children."
"1184","1186 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed marriage to the wife of al-Bara ibn Ma'rur, and she said: I stipulated to my husband that I would not marry after him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is not right."
"1185","103 - Budayl ibn Warqa al-Khuza'i. 1187 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me, that Budayl ibn Bishr ibn Abdullah ibn Salama ibn Budayl ibn Warqa informed him, saying: My grandfather Abdullah ibn Salama informed me, from his father, from Budayl ibn Warqa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered into his alliance on the day of al-Hudaybiya, Khuza'a, and he wrote to them and to Budayl ibn Warqa and the chiefs of Banu Amr: Peace be upon you; I praise to you Allah besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I have not sinned against your alliance, nor have I neglected your side, and the most honourable of the people of Tihama to me are you and those who follow you among the Mutayyabin. And I have secured for those of you who emigrated the same as I secured for myself, even if he emigrated in his land without residing in Mecca, and you are neither to be feared from my side nor to be frightened. This or similar."
"1186","1188 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami al-Misri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Abdullah ibn Salama ibn Budayl ibn Warqa narrated to us, my father Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father Abd al-Rahman, from his father Muhammad ibn Bishr, from his father Bishr ibn Abdullah, from his father Abdullah ibn Salama, from his father Salama ibn Budayl, from his father Budayl ibn Warqa. Salama said: My father Budayl ibn Warqa handed to me this letter and said: O my son, this is the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so keep it well, and you will remain in good as long as it is among you: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Budayl ibn Warqa and Busr and the chiefs of Banu Amr. I praise to you Allah besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I have not sinned against your alliance, nor have I neglected your side, and the most honourable of my family of Tihama to me are you, and the nearest of them to me in kinship, and those who follow you among the Mutayyabin. I have secured for those of you who emigrated the same as I secured for myself, even if he emigrated in his land without residing in Mecca except as one performing Umra or Hajj. And I have not neglected you since I made peace, and you are neither to be feared from my side nor to be confined. To proceed: Alqama ibn Ulatha and the two sons of Hawdha have embraced Islam, and pledged allegiance, and emigrated with those who followed them from Ikrima, and he secured for those who followed them among you the same as he secured for himself, and some are of others forever in sacred and profane times. Abu Muhammad said: And my father narrated to me, saying: I heard our elders saying: It is the handwriting of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1187","1189 - Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Ibn Abi Abla narrated to us, from Ibn Budayl ibn Warqa, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Budayl to detain the captives and the properties at al-Ji'rana until he would come to him, so they were detained."
"1188","104 - Banna al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1190 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr, Jabir ibn Abdullah informed me, that Banna al-Juhani informed him that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people in a mosque who had drawn a sword therein and were passing it among themselves, so he said: May Allah curse whoever did this, did I not forbid you from it? When one of you draws the sword, let him sheathe it, then let him hand it to his companion, likewise."
"1189","105 - Busr, Abu Abdullah al-Mazini. 1191 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, al-Fudayl ibn Fadala narrated to us, that Khalid ibn Ma'dan narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Busr narrated to him that he heard his father Busr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Saturday, saying: If one of you finds nothing except to chew the bark of a tree, then let him not fast on that day. And Abdullah ibn Busr said: If you doubt, then ask my sister. He said: So Khalid ibn Ma'dan walked to her and asked her about what Abdullah mentioned, and she narrated that to him."
"1190","1192 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ibn Abdullah ibn Busr, from his father Abdullah ibn Busr, from his father Busr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them riding on a mule which we used to call a Syrian donkey. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions entered upon them, and my mother stood and placed for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a velvet cloth upon a mat in the house, preferring him with it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon it, it stuck to the mat. Abdullah ibn Busr said: So my father Busr offered them dates to occupy them with, and ordered my mother, so she prepared for them a dish of jashish. Abdullah said: I was the servant between my father and my mother, and my father was attending to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. When my mother finished the jashish, I came carrying it until I placed it before them, and they ate. Then he gave them fadikh to drink, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, and gave drink to the one on his right. Then I took the cup until what was in it ran out, so I filled it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Give it to the one the cup ended at. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the food, he supplicated for us, saying: O Allah, have mercy on them, forgive them, and bless for them in their provision. And we continued to recognise from Allah Almighty abundance in provision."
"1191","106 - Busr ibn Jahhash al-Qurashi, also said to be Bishr. 1193 - Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Yazid al-Hawti and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Mughira Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysara, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Busr ibn Jahhash al-Qurashi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat one day upon his palm, then placed his finger upon it, then said: O son of Adam, Allah Almighty says: You will never render Me incapable, when I created you from the like of this, until when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments, and the earth has a groaning from you, so you gathered and acted, until when it reached the collar bones, you said: Shall I give charity, and when is the time of charity?"
"1192","1194 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, Thawr ibn Yazid al-Rahabi narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysara, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Busr ibn Jahhash, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought out his hand and spat in it, then looked at it, then said: Allah says: How can you render Me incapable, O son of Adam, when I created you only from the like of this, then fashioned you and proportioned you, and you walked between two garments, and the earth has a groaning from you, so you gathered and withheld, until when it reached the collar bones, you said: Shall I give charity now, and when is the time of charity?"
"1193","107 - Busr ibn Abi Artat al-Qurashi, and the name of Abu Artat is Umayr ibn Uwaymir ibn Imran ibn al-Halbas ibn Sinan ibn Nizar ibn Ma'is ibn Amir ibn Lu'ayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr ibn Malik. 1195 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to us, from Shuyaym ibn Baytan, from Junada ibn Abi Umayya, that he said upon the pulpit when he flogged the two men who stole from the spoils of the people: Nothing prevented me from cutting them except Busr ibn Artat, who found a man stealing on campaign and flogged him and did not cut his hand, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from cutting during campaigns."
"1194","1196 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Maysara ibn Halbas narrated to us, saying: I heard my father, who heard Busr ibn Artat, who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, make good my outcome in all matters, and save me from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter."
"1195","1197 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, Uthman ibn Allaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ubayda, from a freedman of the family of Busr, from Busr ibn Artat, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, make good my outcome in all matters, and save me from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter. And he said: Whoever has this as his supplication dies before calamity befalls him."
"1196","1198 - al-Husayn ibn al-Samayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Shayban narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ubayda ibn al-Muhajir, from Yazid, freedman of Busr ibn Artat, from Busr ibn Abi Artat, that he used to supplicate: O Allah, make good our outcome in all matters, and save us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter."
"1197","Chapter of those named Bishr. 108 - Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Ma'rur al-Ansari, of al-Aqaba, of Badr. 1199 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa: Regarding the naming of the companions of al-Aqaba who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu Salama ibn Yazid ibn Jusham: Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Ma'rur, and he witnessed Badr."
"1198","1200 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding those who witnessed al-Aqaba among the Ansar, then from Banu Salama: Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Ma'rur, and he is the one who ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the sheep in which poison was placed on the day of Khaybar."
"1199","1201 - al-Hasan ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Banu Ubayd ibn Adi: Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Ma'rur."
"1200","1202 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that a Jewish woman gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a roasted sheep, and he ate from it, then said: It has informed me that it is poisoned. So Bishr ibn al-Bara died from it, and he sent for her and said: What carried you to do what you did? She said: I wanted to know, if you were a prophet it would not harm you, and if you were a king I would relieve the people of you. So he ordered regarding her and she was killed."
